#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161894 :question/id #uuid "55e8e57f-7f9e-529a-aa1b-24e1d86c4133" :question/math-academy-id "e-9470" :question/problem "![](images/76/765415456d7f33c3558e08e7c4fc01ef3e80961c1e073a210033d91741d78f60.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s,\n$$ where $C$ is the arc of a semicircle of radius $4$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s = L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, $C$ is a semicircle of radius $r = 4.$ Its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L=\\pi r=4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s = 4\\pi.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161895 :question/id #uuid "fdab3229-66ca-59d3-ac20-8a5b3d3506fc" :question/math-academy-id "e-9471" :question/problem "![](images/84/84de7754ed9244e3d646e452f6ed6dab349c130d17eae1d4dbc94cb52bd761e1.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path shown above, traversed once counterclockwise." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of three parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/f4/f4e80a23910612bd55e7578a074f23c76535139889faff479c4dd0521e7496ff.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C = C_1 \\cup C_2 \\cup C_3$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d s =  \\int_{C_1}f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d s + \\int_{C_2}f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d s + \\int_{C_3}f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s = L.\n$$\n\nThe path $C_1$ is a semicircle of radius $r = 3.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_1} \\,\\textrm ds = \\dfrac{1}{2}(2 \\pi r) = 3\\pi.\n$$\n\nThe paths $C_2$ and $C_3$ are hypotenuses of right triangles whose legs have lengths $3$ and $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_2} \\,\\textrm ds = \\int_{C_3} \\,\\textrm ds = \\sqrt{3^2 + 4^2} = 5.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s = 3\\pi + 5 + 5 = 3\\pi + 10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161896 :question/id #uuid "4d5a8f9d-7324-547c-ae5e-b49294debc1b" :question/math-academy-id "e-9472" :question/problem "Consider the curves $C_1$ and $C_2,$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨\\frac{1}{9}{t}^{3},\\,t⟩, & 0\\le t\\le 3 \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨3{u}^{3},\\,3u⟩, & 0\\le u\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose $$\n\\displaystyle\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = k\n$$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = 3k\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = k\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = k\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Notice that $C_1$ and $C_2$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = k.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that $C_1$ and $C_2$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{1}{9}y^3, \\quad 0\\leq y\\leq 3.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds  = \\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162326 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8de278d-ef94-53b3-a37d-10ade572c491" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159159} {:answer/id #uuid "db1ebdeb-d8c2-5ee3-bc75-4945f7199fb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159160} {:answer/id #uuid "feddb339-fa62-5dad-8d5b-8385d20d7d34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159161} {:answer/id #uuid "02c1b5cc-f5dd-5df3-aa07-49600ed22732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159162} {:answer/id #uuid "75d4187a-0ea4-5604-bfd9-c405fec10a64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159163}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4f88280b-5b73-509d-b173-5a9d26ec9781" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159158}] :question/id #uuid "03eb9f6c-5710-543d-af91-9b267957eccb" :question/math-academy-id "q-122478" :question/problem "Suppose $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{C_{1}}f(x, y)ds = 2\n$$ for some function $f(x, y)$, where $C_{1}$ is parametrized by $r_{1}(t) = ⟨t, t^{2}⟩$ for $0 \\le t \\le 1$.\n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n\n1. $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{-C_{1}}f(x, y)ds =-2\n$$\n2. $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{-C_{1}}f(x, y)ds = 2\n$$\n3. $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{C_{2}}f(x, y)ds = 4,\n$$ where $C_{2}$ is parametrized by $r_{2}(u) = ⟨2u, 4u^{2}⟩$ for $0 \\le u \\le \\frac{1}{2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162327 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac6987e-1443-5102-be6c-7c404cb81a29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\pi +1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253751} {:answer/id #uuid "4848d525-4fed-5241-aa55-e8be28361018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(\\pi +2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254286} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb762e8-b607-526d-970c-769c2e97b12a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\pi +2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254526} {:answer/id #uuid "a1ab8300-d36e-5b2f-b815-bf8f3c00e075" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(2\\pi +1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255094} {:answer/id #uuid "f438f0f4-4512-5533-b108-0d1c4c07ad3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(\\pi +1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fb762e8-b607-526d-970c-769c2e97b12a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\pi +2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254526} :answer-field/id #uuid "02208297-3b6c-56a2-86c8-c39f569c53b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ef2f2e1e-2df6-5eea-a523-f7500a9f7301" :question/math-academy-id "q-122481" :question/problem "![](images/55/558dbbc424725ca0d9bad628968489cc2e32d67136102290666ff055a634bc16.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is a path that traverses a semicircle of radius $2$ once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/82/82fedadbb33b1747832bac25d9cda8e0b6b18b0fab411a870e90bc09ce47226e.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is a semi-circle of radius $r=2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\pi r=2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is a line segment of length $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=2\\pi +4=2(\\pi +2).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162328 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "976609f5-9b7b-5cf5-8af9-7eda58f599e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{2} + \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159171} {:answer/id #uuid "f5827111-0006-5c1b-ba8a-12b199fc5f54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "π + 2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159172} {:answer/id #uuid "1e127cda-f337-5d92-a559-58f2b9959529" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "π + \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159173} {:answer/id #uuid "3f7e980f-41b3-58a9-b313-eb4e1299df8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{2} + \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159174} {:answer/id #uuid "68d2396c-897e-51b5-9821-0211bcf63840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2π + 3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159175}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9788a76e-e0cc-5a5d-b125-0a5dce44952b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159170}] :question/id #uuid "e7cfc0f1-43a0-55ae-a985-5e79d8a25ecd" :question/math-academy-id "q-122484" :question/problem "![](images/52/5277642b981910a5da1dd00a1b9aa4db28c7db7fcacf33faf209eea3ec1e93ab.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{C}ds,\n$$ where $C$ is a path that traverses a circular segment of radius $2$ once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162329 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9753b03f-5368-57b2-af6c-e7dbe0c7a32b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159177} {:answer/id #uuid "eb3bba85-4f43-5945-9af3-289916125d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3π}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159178} {:answer/id #uuid "f9beb1c2-834d-5706-a18d-d85e62930916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159179} {:answer/id #uuid "24255bc5-5854-5b3f-b032-26c0628e5e16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159180} {:answer/id #uuid "6d552bcd-423f-5cca-9da0-17c23c691043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159181}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e15c9333-073d-521f-b511-64879ae2fcf0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159176}] :question/id #uuid "644abfce-6167-55c8-a092-efe38481c912" :question/math-academy-id "q-122567" :question/problem "![](images/c5/c5f7ed5a3d4763df369a9bc76cc934e5dd2c7f85dd074f623ae4f59f77f8e0c1.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{C}ds,\n$$ where $C$ is the arc of a semicircle of radius $3$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162330 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95ed31a0-aafb-51f7-ab3d-e8ff5050b401" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159183} {:answer/id #uuid "9e77d5a5-ebf9-5dce-9e8c-ff031c4ef20a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159184} {:answer/id #uuid "a966c171-289b-5056-80b1-a3a81a3dff1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159185} {:answer/id #uuid "1ee86563-d77d-5365-bfcf-19085bedd792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159186} {:answer/id #uuid "299d46ee-11e3-5c2a-8729-11f0f4e10517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159187}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8cc74610-e88e-565b-911f-e91506b49f46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159182}] :question/id #uuid "c6541032-7a7a-5a1c-bb3c-d0a7d3bd3d1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122571" :question/problem "Consider the curves $C_{1}$ and $C_{2}$, defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\hspace{1em}{\\mathbf{r}}_{1}(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}t,\\hspace{0.222em}\\operatorname{cos}t⟩, & 0\\le t\\le 2\\pi  \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\hspace{1em}{\\mathbf{r}}_{2}(\\theta ) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}2\\theta ,\\hspace{0.222em}\\operatorname{cos}2\\theta ⟩, & 0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{C_{1}}f(x, y)ds = k\n$$ for some function $f(x, y)$ and real number $k$. Which of the following must be true?\n\n1. $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{-C_{1}}f(x, y)ds = k\n$$\n2. $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{C_{2}}f(x, y)ds = k\n$$\n3. $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{C_{2}}f(x, y)ds = \\frac{1}{2}k\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42d6a148-88c2-5e27-b2b8-7077e4ee92a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254242} {:answer/id #uuid "5e89e2cb-53fb-5209-b3b3-97fdcea9c2f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254511} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c3c401-a416-5d33-9269-e60113197301" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255400} {:answer/id #uuid "cf6c7463-ebe9-5c33-a220-becd6222ffaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255515} {:answer/id #uuid "f05c2444-815f-56de-b32a-4ff4cd4ae7c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42d6a148-88c2-5e27-b2b8-7077e4ee92a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254242} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8f24811-145c-5e38-85a4-66faa4942fa5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "418cd3d5-ecfd-5690-a4c6-98dd1a3d29e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-122768" :question/problem "![](images/b7/b7e72ce1ab38408f04f3b8d5a228ec0a3632c60086ef0a7abeb7e18af3002e6b.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $3$ and $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256713 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ff0acc0-0e93-5334-be16-87734e65f347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253947} {:answer/id #uuid "267a1756-880b-503d-9cde-ec448304a42a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254013} {:answer/id #uuid "3916ee0d-ef52-5786-a7a9-672356d765a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254166} {:answer/id #uuid "5356d693-3c5b-5b4b-a259-9f59cf7f89fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254397} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b78f71-4853-5da1-a1f0-3fedc3d3c1bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5356d693-3c5b-5b4b-a259-9f59cf7f89fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254397} :answer-field/id #uuid "38593efc-6c98-5f7c-a0ed-dbed4bca04a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5a8b286f-d065-50b6-ae53-27022484f1f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-122766" :question/problem "![](images/1a/1a46390ced6cc52c535f9f48e5e157cea83960caa339e98b23e3b64c93e0ea38.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is a line segment directed along the $y$-axis. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=3-(-1)=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256714 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57b9b426-71c1-5edb-9dd9-ca085fb61738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254441} {:answer/id #uuid "77ea77f7-6a1b-56e7-8f3b-74939f184252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254729} {:answer/id #uuid "8943a84b-b99d-54fe-9fb1-3ac026d3d430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254887} {:answer/id #uuid "b2a7cf28-d7d6-5020-81cc-adfd50ba234f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255243} {:answer/id #uuid "cf01093d-6c43-52d5-8c1a-7fdd0ec9b92e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2a7cf28-d7d6-5020-81cc-adfd50ba234f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255243} :answer-field/id #uuid "589066a3-615a-51c9-bb5d-9e742c10db6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256092}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3baa811b-dfdb-522b-86b9-2539a33b41e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-122767" :question/problem "![](images/d8/d82f445e19af6e6d343bfab6c082108e945a8feb21caa9b60a2d93da24fc3f6a.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the line segment directed along the $x$-axis. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=5-1=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256715 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ce7ca60-5bcd-5786-a176-79dc33c37a12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254197} {:answer/id #uuid "614d3299-5ff7-52bc-9ff5-8dea36b35628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254542} {:answer/id #uuid "8fd81a7e-ee4a-5467-8b4d-882cd76a5836" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254932} {:answer/id #uuid "bb63d7d5-a184-535e-a55e-59071a4a779c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255340} {:answer/id #uuid "d7cde993-b01f-5a5f-ac2a-e34925aad9ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "614d3299-5ff7-52bc-9ff5-8dea36b35628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254542} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a12dd65-6b67-5890-bee5-c40b46175718" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "65bfb8fc-d1de-55fb-a552-bcd799264edb" :question/math-academy-id "q-122769" :question/problem "![](images/e4/e41579712730d26c66d9f46f8d978fd51c8efbd76394c094113454e24b3aaff7.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $2$ and $4:$ \n\n![](images/84/849f44d06de55f14811d433f9ccfdd30d47f6a1db1970cdfbfbd6f16be4959b0.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=2\\sqrt{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256716 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a61e51f-0cb8-563b-a933-412b31a8bff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253894} {:answer/id #uuid "2f133303-0ca9-5c34-9b67-603238077a30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254086} {:answer/id #uuid "60d04bd9-3b2b-5773-af0c-28cc3399b1c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254536} {:answer/id #uuid "6662b8b2-0b86-5153-b706-d142f59cd08d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254592} {:answer/id #uuid "7e3cc7a1-a0b3-5270-a27e-c99b62538255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60d04bd9-3b2b-5773-af0c-28cc3399b1c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254536} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c66c1de-5cc3-594e-9c4d-492721e5ecfe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "10f80d39-efd4-5625-821a-21dfccdb41c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-122770" :question/problem "![](images/69/69072873cb1f613ee9c2fa4a4caf3dc3409026c2a8310847b1c3dd890cc816d8.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $3$ and $6:$ \n\n![](images/d0/d0d9f0fad038f04b6d93920979161694f4e709a31b68083f20e768bf60aa1675.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{45} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=3\\sqrt{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256721 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b877064-2518-5f0a-b4cc-e8ce3cdb6339" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462061} {:answer/id #uuid "d31ab5cc-8f03-565c-baa7-182f415d2e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b877064-2518-5f0a-b4cc-e8ce3cdb6339" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462061} :answer-field/id #uuid "a889bc2a-6c37-5857-b5df-2f84c3f8a657" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462784} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4072d32e-8787-592f-a6a0-ab69807057af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462063} {:answer/id #uuid "119a56a7-be8a-525d-bf38-85a10b27e983" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4072d32e-8787-592f-a6a0-ab69807057af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462063} :answer-field/id #uuid "115eacf4-2515-53aa-bfd6-ab8ce878fbab" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=8,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(u)=⟨16{u}^{4}-12{u}^{2},\\,2u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462785} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac676307-c5cf-59c4-8590-312fc31f883c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462065} {:answer/id #uuid "298a07b4-50d6-5be9-96f1-5114af5fa7ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "298a07b4-50d6-5be9-96f1-5114af5fa7ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462066} :answer-field/id #uuid "99e4091b-8534-5001-a586-9ba94089c8a0" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462786}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5b1e210e-8810-5093-9deb-eb8812e9311b" :question/math-academy-id "q-122814" :question/problem "Suppose $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4\n$$ for some function $f(x,y),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(t)=⟨{t}^{4}-3{t}^{2},\\,t⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le 2.$\n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-4\n$$ is false, while statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4\n$$ is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=8,\n$$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(u)=⟨16{u}^{4}-12{u}^{2},\\,2u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1.$” is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx={y}^{4}-3{y}^{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256722 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d69ae25e-4067-57d7-992a-aea277568ec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462067} {:answer/id #uuid "738c6bee-a025-5815-b191-c51eede9211c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d69ae25e-4067-57d7-992a-aea277568ec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462067} :answer-field/id #uuid "c61b6f96-e8f3-53f9-b0c0-da26da3e6072" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=2,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le \\pi .$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462787} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4efe198-1a08-51cc-bb7f-57e8f0ee8eb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462069} {:answer/id #uuid "51e47506-7d0a-5b3e-b515-61f96ae37f6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4efe198-1a08-51cc-bb7f-57e8f0ee8eb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462069} :answer-field/id #uuid "5edbd1d2-7f0f-56a6-b340-a1ec1e119077" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462788} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bba662d-b093-5629-b0a1-c818e13f06a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462071} {:answer/id #uuid "cad3636b-9235-5c64-8894-54bc8fd1a1b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cad3636b-9235-5c64-8894-54bc8fd1a1b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462072} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3bdd892-fdc2-556f-bf24-620230aff8e4" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "533221ac-cdcc-53a5-adcd-03f57c6b1b57" :question/math-academy-id "q-122815" :question/problem "Suppose $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1\n$$ for some function $f(x,y),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by $$\n\\displaystyle {r}_{1}(u)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{u}{2}\\right),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{u}{2}\\right)⟩\n$$ for $0\\le u\\le 2\\pi .$ \n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=2,\n$$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le \\pi .$” is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we note that both parameterizations traverse a half-circle of radius $1$ centered at $O$ between $0$ and $\\pi .$\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-1\n$$ is false, while statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1\n$$ is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256723 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e05ec3e-cd64-5efe-b86c-3a85d32445a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462073} {:answer/id #uuid "555ded60-6e27-5822-bfad-111ae26de821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "555ded60-6e27-5822-bfad-111ae26de821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462074} :answer-field/id #uuid "570b3d91-151c-5000-a5f6-67a9b778db1d" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462790} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce53e294-37f1-5e16-892e-9c87da353bbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462075} {:answer/id #uuid "2fecce07-97ed-543c-9956-f750f8ecd7a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce53e294-37f1-5e16-892e-9c87da353bbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462075} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c544999-5092-5e3f-ba7a-7f9b6e161fa2" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462791} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d78c6e8e-5d8a-5dfc-b896-579c21a26b8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462077} {:answer/id #uuid "60092f97-7805-566d-a27b-a35ee30d9698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d78c6e8e-5d8a-5dfc-b896-579c21a26b8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462077} :answer-field/id #uuid "6319433e-b1e6-54c4-9ece-69e71614667d" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=12,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(u)=⟨4u,\\,8{u}^{3/2}⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462792}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "aba31fa9-c0e0-5ac2-bdfd-ad58b74f6f1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-122816" :question/problem "Suppose $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3\n$$ for some function $f(x,y),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(t)=⟨t,\\,{t}^{3/2}⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le 4.$\n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3\n$$ is true, while statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-3\n$$ is false. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=12,\n$$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(u)=⟨4u,\\,8{u}^{3/2}⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1.$” is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\ny={x}^{3/2},\\,0\\le x\\le 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256725 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "461a27ae-9bae-56e4-a290-8a9b99dd2f96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254262} {:answer/id #uuid "48f7a64a-5065-5b48-9afa-0c3ec86372c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254296} {:answer/id #uuid "7fa5f20e-2e73-5f1c-9c2f-9b1fb94075b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254799} {:answer/id #uuid "8b6906ae-426e-569c-adc9-44144d8e41a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254901} {:answer/id #uuid "a3313bd1-e6b1-51a4-ba38-134097b446aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fa5f20e-2e73-5f1c-9c2f-9b1fb94075b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254799} :answer-field/id #uuid "37cd5012-6b1d-57b4-a60a-c7978b2ab3f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256019}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "23524215-604c-5fbd-8acf-4af9e94c29ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-122828" :question/problem "![](images/39/39a7cb0b31cb5d906803063597ae968be8fba90f048a4d9745225de7c3f8d6db.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of three parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/05/058c7b33112329df321e61660df4f2d388f42ca40c0aae5b73a089a0251726e2.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe paths ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are line segments of length $3.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{3}}\\,\\text{d}s=3.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $3$ and $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=3+5+3=11.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256730 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48070546-d80f-5246-86a4-aa8d7aa99c50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254279} {:answer/id #uuid "72a7d010-8a49-501c-a8b0-6c4408fdf75f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254685} {:answer/id #uuid "96002547-d724-56a8-8e09-188ad7369cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi +4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254992} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1a64fc-def5-5882-88a7-756a23766b42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255336} {:answer/id #uuid "c24b4875-c3c0-55e6-b7fe-e4f60d7affdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72a7d010-8a49-501c-a8b0-6c4408fdf75f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254685} :answer-field/id #uuid "01fb92ac-5f7f-5736-aab9-a7276e24a517" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255920}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f87f9aea-995d-5fa2-9903-84aef89b9be9" :question/math-academy-id "q-122843" :question/problem "![](images/d7/d7844777c0bb540ba337756f45c4d71a8a8e9f9c84372e01542892801efecce3.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/98/98f444851e2df505d4242d1f8e4be0d76f78babd5d9633d9ab0ec84c245fe364.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is three-quarters of a circle of radius $r=2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{3}{4}(2\\pi r)=3\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is a line segment of length $2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=3\\pi +2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256731 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2461d307-3086-5a5c-b497-aa48ad65c133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253997} {:answer/id #uuid "2dbd98bc-e62d-5a92-bfa0-9c4e1787b547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(2+\\sqrt{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254082} {:answer/id #uuid "65e5a51e-ba13-5ae9-a263-385c9c9cf5de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(3+\\sqrt{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254582} {:answer/id #uuid "a1016a1d-d5a6-5066-9d4a-cb08a1cf0136" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5+2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255084} {:answer/id #uuid "b2237b88-2d33-5dfc-a776-cc65d79f2e63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1016a1d-d5a6-5066-9d4a-cb08a1cf0136" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5+2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255084} :answer-field/id #uuid "a64d136c-2e50-5fe9-8693-5b8666a0d0be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256225}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "efd8621e-7cbb-5240-b849-bfa0535c815e" :question/math-academy-id "q-122845" :question/problem "![](images/68/68b3f78c29c9d7776efc2a78672ae53fe2e806d7ca6c3d663de8a16c03342132.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/27/27c19b56a24315f1105539afc441a33957dddf606b3410b86121e7cb8ed16973.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $3$ and $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}=5.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $2$ and $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}}=2\\sqrt{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=5+2\\sqrt{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256733 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06fbccd3-1730-54fc-9475-ad997c5afc37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi +4\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253721} {:answer/id #uuid "21e53e95-7ec4-5c95-b9e3-453c9a2ed4f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(2\\pi +\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253974} {:answer/id #uuid "44332bd0-327e-53e0-9733-797aa948733d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi +4\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254249} {:answer/id #uuid "6169a709-a992-502e-9cbc-f73991286538" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254543} {:answer/id #uuid "819bf68a-c423-5c96-b729-706e6eb1fc6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\pi +2\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "819bf68a-c423-5c96-b729-706e6eb1fc6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\pi +2\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254817} :answer-field/id #uuid "4639a58d-2fdb-5f66-8101-7eaad8afbbd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256053}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "65d60feb-29ba-53eb-9de0-464deb1c4c60" :question/math-academy-id "q-122850" :question/problem "![](images/bf/bf87c4707c0f4a8ab1b5157a13e8c7785da915833c5f9d896a2747af27f70e59.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/ff/ff52b8e83a9cc9867b25ea3c24ed0f988a27dec73f9e0ab2dfda28ddabb3238a.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path shown above.\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is a quarter of a circle of radius $r=4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{1}{4}(2\\pi r)=2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle where both legs have a length of $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}}=4\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=2\\pi +4\\sqrt{2}=2(\\pi +2\\sqrt{2}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256734 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "756cdc53-2932-5002-93f3-0e049675c868" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462079} {:answer/id #uuid "c481b00c-7230-5985-9e66-4d8b6087f4e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "756cdc53-2932-5002-93f3-0e049675c868" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462079} :answer-field/id #uuid "a52e79c6-6b76-598b-a0c0-137e3101dc68" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462793} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0be94117-938f-5e8d-b8dc-23f5959ac80d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462081} {:answer/id #uuid "d62869e1-04c3-5ef3-b5f6-f5bbc804f3f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0be94117-938f-5e8d-b8dc-23f5959ac80d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462081} :answer-field/id #uuid "da261af8-d4c1-56bf-8d02-1b93eb8f0515" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{2k}{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462794} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d76ae1f0-3cf0-5980-8be4-9864329b561e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462083} {:answer/id #uuid "668a58f5-744b-5464-a0b3-4a5197e2f210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "668a58f5-744b-5464-a0b3-4a5197e2f210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462084} :answer-field/id #uuid "b55baf9c-63c9-5110-ad82-91c7b4d263f7" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "67eba06b-e142-51bc-86cf-6cd55545886d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122851" :question/problem "Consider the curves ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2},$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+1},\\,3t⟩, & 0\\le t\\le \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+1},\\,2u⟩, & 0\\le u\\le \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k\n$$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-k\n$$ is false. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{2k}{3}\n$$ is false, while statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k\n$$ is true. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+1},\\,0\\le y\\le 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256735 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d626c071-0c70-52ac-bc79-16a2a3cf5cad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462085} {:answer/id #uuid "db1e1ca4-1a4a-5645-912d-ad584f2b5ce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db1e1ca4-1a4a-5645-912d-ad584f2b5ce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462086} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f97f6d4-1cc7-5a18-9002-6bc12e80f56c" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462796} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8ec0988-8d3b-58bb-8f11-a31026537190" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462087} {:answer/id #uuid "7122ea47-8dea-506b-a7e9-89375fe1971b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8ec0988-8d3b-58bb-8f11-a31026537190" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462087} :answer-field/id #uuid "3eccce40-3459-5071-bdd9-96e4fe102f63" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=2k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462797} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cd90f72-67c5-5198-8924-c359511557f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462089} {:answer/id #uuid "97613da4-4123-53e9-ac7f-e007a645737b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97613da4-4123-53e9-ac7f-e007a645737b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462090} :answer-field/id #uuid "56e9d11d-7777-5fe2-9ce3-8596ef406783" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "261c6852-f708-5ef6-9e89-3d88f4dbba8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-122868" :question/problem "Consider the curves ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2},$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨2t,\\,2\\sqrt{t}⟩, & 0\\le t\\le 2 \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨4u,\\,2\\sqrt{2u}⟩, & 0\\le u\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k\n$$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k\n$$ is true, while statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=2k\n$$ is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{2x},\\,0\\le x\\le 4.\n$$\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k\n$$ is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k;\n$$ $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521880 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27cae781-a5b1-5d1a-a336-28677997d8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521883} {:answer/id #uuid "43adf706-556a-5541-95dd-e56f093e98a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27cae781-a5b1-5d1a-a336-28677997d8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521883} :answer-field/id #uuid "300668c7-94d5-5a1d-96ad-33fc31a43286" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521885} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e4dc9fc-e868-51af-82a5-75a6f7