\,\\text{d}s=k\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521905 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54b68761-81ae-5727-8723-99155f456d21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521896} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e75279-2f6c-585f-a49b-30410cd91345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54b68761-81ae-5727-8723-99155f456d21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521896} :answer-field/id #uuid "353ba0ff-733c-57e5-8e81-74317481335b" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{5k}{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521887} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03178fdc-25eb-592a-aa45-4e266963dfb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521877} {:answer/id #uuid "f9cde8a0-0128-565a-a4cd-433dec39fb80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9cde8a0-0128-565a-a4cd-433dec39fb80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521925} :answer-field/id #uuid "84208a78-46f7-5cc8-aae2-ed3bf108cc3d" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521903} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6080977b-5766-59b3-82b0-9891037d1857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521899} {:answer/id #uuid "f5c7ad3d-6caa-593c-b2d1-652348ed0ede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5c7ad3d-6caa-593c-b2d1-652348ed0ede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521922} :answer-field/id #uuid "a38cc838-6019-5577-98f0-f639569b05e7" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521908}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8b2a59b4-567e-519b-bf4b-185eb8ce7675" :question/problem "Consider the curves ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2},$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}+6},\\,4t⟩, & 0\\le t\\le \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨\\sqrt{25{u}^{2}+6},\\,5u⟩, & 0\\le u\\le \\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k\n$$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-k\n$$ is false. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{5k}{4}\n$$ is false, while statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k\n$$ is true. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+6},\\,0\\le y\\le 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521916 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12383e44-707a-5bdc-aed6-bacd5d241604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521881} {:answer/id #uuid "d39317c7-f550-51db-95fa-14ecef4d8119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12383e44-707a-5bdc-aed6-bacd5d241604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521881} :answer-field/id #uuid "2849e85a-9324-5c9e-8606-379763c5280c" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(u)=⟨243{u}^{4}-18{u}^{2},\\,3u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521884} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66fdd48e-d5d5-5dab-826a-ac4be0dd2146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521900} {:answer/id #uuid "f63ced98-a9ce-5a73-aa16-45250abe7b46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f63ced98-a9ce-5a73-aa16-45250abe7b46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521923} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b47340d-4902-5241-a3d9-513d7bd87af2" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521895} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2c947ff-8de3-54d5-9100-bb93fe81f325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521921} {:answer/id #uuid "f7971d96-ca08-549f-84cc-5b72709d09cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7971d96-ca08-549f-84cc-5b72709d09cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521924} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcd179a6-c2d5-5420-98bf-79fb4b48750e" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d7163cdf-b4ca-5487-945d-916df17c97fc" :question/problem "Suppose $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1\n$$ for some function $f(x,y),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(t)=⟨3{t}^{4}-2{t}^{2},\\,t⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le 3.$\n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-1\n$$ is false, while statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1\n$$ is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3,\n$$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(u)=⟨243{u}^{4}-18{u}^{2},\\,3u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1.$” is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx=3{y}^{4}-2{y}^{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521917 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a9f9a52-3082-5433-95a4-c5f4c8ae8cd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521897} {:answer/id #uuid "e91b5391-28fc-5690-8b2d-39d3a871a375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a9f9a52-3082-5433-95a4-c5f4c8ae8cd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521897} :answer-field/id #uuid "1993f2eb-5838-569b-889b-81d0a604df5e" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521882} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3df0d4d-09b8-5201-b83b-666c7581491b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521909} {:answer/id #uuid "fbf41162-0ae6-5fde-a058-b41d64e5185f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbf41162-0ae6-5fde-a058-b41d64e5185f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521926} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fd61f71-05fe-55f1-b853-74a722e4ca24" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=16,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(u)=⟨768{u}^{4}-64{u}^{2},\\,4u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521906} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b1d7ba5-ad3e-5ada-b964-6c10ca778eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521894} {:answer/id #uuid "847b701e-4db4-558f-93db-2cb8924742bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "847b701e-4db4-558f-93db-2cb8924742bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521904} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7dc35ec-2dc1-528e-a10f-cea74dd734d7" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dc964df5-3846-54bf-91a3-d8d19abd4103" :question/problem "Suppose $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4\n$$ for some function $f(x,y),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(t)=⟨3{t}^{4}-4{t}^{2},\\,t⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le 4.$\n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-4\n$$ is false, while statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4\n$$ is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=16,\n$$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(u)=⟨768{u}^{4}-64{u}^{2},\\,4u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1.$” is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx=3{y}^{4}-4{y}^{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543730 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e392493-12b7-5fff-a789-f4a3cf5d01f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543751} {:answer/id #uuid "9aa03926-e900-5999-9093-1d000b69385d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3361}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543772} {:answer/id #uuid "ce794cd4-db55-56f9-b983-5fa880a1168a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{71}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543786} {:answer/id #uuid "d0828197-5b40-5c68-b0ea-1f4bd3d201a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3361}{144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543788} {:answer/id #uuid "f4e59bea-6a7a-5534-bc03-1d74041599c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9aa03926-e900-5999-9093-1d000b69385d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3361}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543772} :answer-field/id #uuid "cee9cae6-cf06-57f3-b029-c631c50e218a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543787}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "10e20319-dae6-5423-9e86-a7cc0396d858" :question/problem "![](images/1f/1fef351611744d83aac26742bada76ee0eb7f4beef06698d8b4b02061aa8045b.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $\\frac{14}{3}$ and $\\frac{5}{4}:$ \n\n![](images/d6/d64fa6b26b1730514b90b28989773cd8996b8deda2dd80bece2e48def3859320.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{\\frac{14}{3}}^{2}+{\\frac{5}{4}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{196}{9}+\\frac{25}{16}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3361}{144}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3361}}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{\\sqrt{3361}}{12}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543741 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44cb5b46-005a-5f87-87e4-036f25b9cd2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543746} {:answer/id #uuid "88fb679f-fc25-5e1a-8a27-a1730abf8244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{45}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543766} {:answer/id #uuid "8a51efa8-e7f2-509d-90dc-60a88a56f276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543767} {:answer/id #uuid "991b214a-0e87-5f60-bf23-f046455dd48d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543770} {:answer/id #uuid "b21afb2d-be8a-572b-b7a0-4255289dca17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44cb5b46-005a-5f87-87e4-036f25b9cd2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543746} :answer-field/id #uuid "e32da741-eca2-5c8f-ae7d-524df68a247b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "364181e6-6962-5fb8-9d2f-01c181d8615e" :question/problem "![](images/fd/fdccb48ecbf30257f5dce2b1d8f9be79cfbc945ed804f0ceef75e519c0292f23.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $\\frac{3}{2}$ and $\\frac{9}{2}:$ \n\n![](images/3a/3ab15ec00cb05ea65a36d59f88246cb56347ea6dc61ff2e589882a4ab92f1919.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{\\frac{3}{2}}^{2}+{\\frac{9}{2}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{81}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{45}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543748 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08d7bcfc-4852-5169-8210-4388508ffdd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543729} {:answer/id #uuid "81deb0bc-0a70-56f9-9b3b-1cf10ef37f1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{91}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543763} {:answer/id #uuid "952b20c2-980e-51b8-83f0-51f7734026ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{4201}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543768} {:answer/id #uuid "d2ee4a8e-4a67-5ae2-97fe-293394c49867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4201}{144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543789} {:answer/id #uuid "e58c2192-77b6-5422-a995-4b958050f4c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "952b20c2-980e-51b8-83f0-51f7734026ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{4201}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543768} :answer-field/id #uuid "9910d54c-f4c9-5159-9e04-6c3f45ac5f71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543769}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4537cc16-16af-5bdb-8f98-6980c39f7768" :question/problem "![](images/c5/c515af7e27657f8bbf832fd35ed69989eb3c7655e1b16b4157b6dc101e827f32.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $\\frac{10}{3}$ and $\\frac{17}{4}:$ \n\n![](images/7c/7cd1670a27c1d84aea03718ca99d611caa825bcc2f16b9955dd35f3106325c87.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{\\frac{10}{3}}^{2}+{\\frac{17}{4}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{100}{9}+\\frac{289}{16}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{4201}{144}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{4201}}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{\\sqrt{4201}}{12}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543752 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a371b33-335c-5a3e-9652-95e51004d231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{1249}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543771} {:answer/id #uuid "a4ab8238-7100-5bfa-98a8-c0f64c68888f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543774} {:answer/id #uuid "c35bd3a0-64fb-5173-8cd0-99efbcf79d23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543780} {:answer/id #uuid "c5668466-715b-5921-8cb9-e00a35d2d351" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{47}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543781} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc325ee-fd76-5ee3-a984-bd8b13ff22d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1249}{144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a371b33-335c-5a3e-9652-95e51004d231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{1249}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543771} :answer-field/id #uuid "db08abd7-7ac3-5e0a-936a-9fd2f8b7d9bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "52e24297-4e2d-5fdb-8d08-a3caad3b97c9" :question/problem "![](images/61/61c9e7095d0b1dfdc2b302a5ca916d05f6a6dcad206be5eb67550246213a9743.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $\\frac{5}{4}$ and $\\frac{8}{3}:$ \n\n![](images/2d/2d17bae26ea31dc9b70309cb56781b054c3086e21f5fbbb642e85c231ae5b451.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{\\frac{5}{4}}^{2}+{\\frac{8}{3}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{16}+\\frac{64}{9}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1249}{144}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{1249}}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{\\sqrt{1249}}{12}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543764 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d3ef204-40b0-55bb-9095-76c79b5e21d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543738} {:answer/id #uuid "2dee75ba-3484-565e-8dfa-38f5b7f933b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{346}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186