\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{\\sqrt{346}}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543777 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "316ce5ff-2b2d-5a76-a504-5da76b6bae14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{53}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543740} {:answer/id #uuid "5cfa77ed-460d-5170-9131-65786d275186" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543754} {:answer/id #uuid "74a78695-1da4-5039-b572-c9d72f93c924" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543760} {:answer/id #uuid "c8164c72-577a-5921-a317-1d948a4aeed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543783} {:answer/id #uuid "d70cf646-0c7f-5a0f-87df-6f8a83bbea45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8164c72-577a-5921-a317-1d948a4aeed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543783} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4812293-b48d-5da8-b5dd-7a8ccc7895dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543791}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b0f1730e-091f-5c51-a8d8-22da3962b13d" :question/problem "![](images/b7/b7794ce7bf86aa14413b940e250fe4c3f07281375a86bac58274e030eef5d97c.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $\\frac{5}{2}$ and $\\frac{9}{2}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{\\frac{5}{2}}^{2}+{\\frac{9}{2}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{4}+\\frac{81}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{53}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543790 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1642d82e-aaf4-5dc7-b840-fd605481d7d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{9553}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543732} {:answer/id #uuid "3be4d6b3-5d17-572c-90b2-27db2fe2d8e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543742} {:answer/id #uuid "68da3236-b33a-54f3-9680-824859e6c87e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{125}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543756} {:answer/id #uuid "7485f311-4668-53e6-8a59-a539e0d485f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543759} {:answer/id #uuid "afbe321e-939b-56c9-817f-01610d34b2c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9553}{144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1642d82e-aaf4-5dc7-b840-fd605481d7d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{9553}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543732} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a358841-d73c-50e0-9845-45c9af1c42f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d3ed05b5-6528-573b-b8fa-1a394e140cfd" :question/problem "![](images/10/10bfa8282f54053e0ec26a51754a90ac3c21cff7dd084419fa1838209c6cad51.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $\\frac{23}{3}$ and $\\frac{11}{4}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{\\frac{23}{3}}^{2}+{\\frac{11}{4}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{529}{9}+\\frac{121}{16}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9553}{144}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{9553}}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{\\sqrt{9553}}{12}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543792 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4459196f-8a17-5bbf-897d-615c14ead4d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{77}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543745} {:answer/id #uuid "46915344-85f3-5142-8935-3b5a242bd7d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3649}{144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543749} {:answer/id #uuid "4bf7171c-2a7b-5214-adba-7a9d3dac5fcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543750} {:answer/id #uuid "84af3719-2da8-55dc-ab55-d173ffecccf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3649}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543765} {:answer/id #uuid "b0c8623e-5089-534e-aff8-4c6b1531b482" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84af3719-2da8-55dc-ab55-d173ffecccf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3649}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543765} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cc121c4-7a4a-534a-b7f9-5b712db4c8df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d4d23703-07d6-5b36-acbf-8a840f8b031e" :question/problem "![](images/6a/6a0ad3faf8dfa0944c8b43c3c5b6c4241f485cb2242aa5a5628c5f0cd7dbf568.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $\\frac{19}{4}$ and $\\frac{5}{3}:$ \n\n![](images/13/1344f3eb2a0c530da734ae8d72e30a776d5ae4e2e8be93f24a1c123f257a5e5c.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{\\frac{19}{4}}^{2}+{\\frac{5}{3}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{361}{16}+\\frac{25}{9}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3649}{144}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3649}}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{\\sqrt{3649}}{12}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543794 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26a40055-2c56-53b7-962f-9513656c0725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543735} {:answer/id #uuid "7c55f915-fbcd-5e4c-bc8a-a0a163a0b9c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543762} {:answer/id #uuid "c700afdb-0746-5bf4-be55-0d51eefd285f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543782} {:answer/id #uuid "cb240005-5b90-54eb-8c61-5f1555a4e87a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{149}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543784} {:answer/id #uuid "e183bec7-a913-5d8c-8041-2217e1272b78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{298}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e183bec7-a913-5d8c-8041-2217e1272b78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{298}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543797} :answer-field/id #uuid "78e43622-9421-5ef4-b0aa-5362255966c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d957a74a-90d5-5573-858f-1a5dad5d66f8" :question/problem "![](images/64/64fad0fb0fce8784fcb390bbd01fa86558191c02677d9f7f618fa97e11787e8b.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $\\frac{3}{2}$ and $\\frac{17}{2}:$ \n\n![](images/d3/d391ea874021dc2d55e158a9a0fc5471caab15dad0dedeee16c4c9aa32066c5c.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{\\frac{3}{2}}^{2}+{\\frac{17}{2}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{289}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{149}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{298}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{\\sqrt{298}}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543799 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "141b04a5-95ff-5e8f-89d4-89018ec5ed3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543731} {:answer/id #uuid "1a05f5c0-053d-563c-9455-6fed01a6acf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543733} {:answer/id #uuid "7295c22b-d98c-5d62-aa75-65aed2ee7b8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{157}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543758} {:answer/id #uuid "df5212a1-a699-55d0-a0bc-daf012979f8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{314}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543796} {:answer/id #uuid "ff23cbd1-0a67-54ae-8a50-d6a0d23aecfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df5212a1-a699-55d0-a0bc-daf012979f8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{314}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543796} :answer-field/id #uuid "6612a747-3cd8-5a2c-a3d2-e364a3b8f6ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543755}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e3d1be88-150b-5f14-913f-6b68318755da" :question/problem "![](images/18/184a128aa9cd2c21049f72eff286c08d128a5fee3d9a716d984369c6fee21278.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $\\frac{17}{2}$ and $\\frac{5}{2}:$ \n\n![](images/ac/ac98d9896020e1cc8708b62d6ceeac3e7edcd2ce39ee6ef60dbbe89100b2b8d2.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{\\frac{17}{2}}^{2}+{\\frac{5}{2}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{289}{4}+\\frac{25}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{157}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{314}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{\\sqrt{314}}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543801 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "078dc799-523b-5bbc-a06e-b73097fc8574" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543728} {:answer/id #uuid "26cc1f82-efdb-5093-ac2f-9c31baa4a784" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543736} {:answer/id #uuid "3c35cfa5-9c6f-5783-b74d-6844f1b6a364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543743} {:answer/id #uuid "53e796c8-568a-551b-87c9-aa92b93a33a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{85}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543753} {:answer/id #uuid "f9090f52-8e55-5562-b825-81ea0a5d6ecb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53e796c8-568a-551b-87c9-aa92b93a33a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{85}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543753} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f82a27e-a9f6-5e22-abd0-8d89910cf32d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ea05930e-fc4b-5ce3-8181-3ec67304640f" :question/problem "![](images/38/388a18afaef104f8036ae6ca36786fada32fa614c724c5f5bd8f3c225a9b7286.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $2$ and $9.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{9}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+81} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{85} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{85}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{85}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564664 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "254fa1aa-2b59-5f26-9246-2796d0242d88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{34 \\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564662} {:answer/id #uuid "69047681-a0ac-5878-89be-37d0746b4773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17 \\pi}{3} + \\frac{68 \\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564684} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf06456-320d-5f63-b850-aadf56a721fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{34 \\sqrt{2}}{3} + \\frac{17 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564694} {:answer/id #uuid "9b7245fc-213e-5e3a-abbd-9bb84f1cd564" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{34 \\sqrt{2}}{3} + \\frac{34 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564700} {:answer/id #uuid "aba8edfe-1ccf-5995-838b-b23e5342af2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cf06456-320d-5f63-b850-aadf56a721fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{34 \\sqrt{2}}{3} + \\frac{17 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564694} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ff80886-22b6-53e7-ab56-0ffaeda80cae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2bd95eb6-ed23-59fb-b84e-91c27fd5bc8c" :question/problem "![](images/42/42e881f2fea91ee9191c5b32dce49f485977ded98a9e900bfcaf51fc1e0f8ec1.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/49/494158fe124fe1c8e1f7f618695dc9846991bd074b199a45a5874ddb8ad16e86.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path shown above.\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is a quarter of a circle of radius $r=\\frac{34}{3}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{1}{4}(2\\pi r)=\\frac{17 \\pi}{3} .\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle where both legs have a length of $\\frac{34}{3}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{\\frac{34}{3}}^{2}+{\\frac{34}{3}}^{2}}=\\frac{34 \\sqrt{2}}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{17 \\pi}{3}+\\frac{34 \\sqrt{2}}{3}=\\frac{17}{3}(\\pi+2\\sqrt{2}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564668 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a4026ea-c30a-5983-ad0c-bd822a8dc3e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564656} {:answer/id #uuid "6b37a7a3-5ba5-5693-8604-1ffbd07065d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564685} {:answer/id #uuid "8ddab92d-89a6-5d3b-b0c5-a6454796a085" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{38}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564696} {:answer/id #uuid "95e2ebbb-303d-51c2-9cdb-29978e161196" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564698} {:answer/id #uuid "f63dbde9-05aa-5d77-8273-3853668871e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{22}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f63dbde9-05aa-5d77-8273-3853668871e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{22}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564721} :answer-field/id #uuid "de148ad0-dd56-5670-9ba2-8c76650d62dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564714}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "37e815a8-9354-5afd-b1c1-eadfdb328f5e" :question/problem "![](images/00/00c1e8199146ddfdc1d8243eccfc5d5f44f9e67474722365a5c39c4a2226dcab.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of three parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/a0/a0fbd1bc9dfacd406a027a0178d223dc972379a6b370b121f28975c345696f85.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe paths ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are line segments of length $2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{3}}\\,\\text{d}s=2.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $2$ and $\\frac{8}{3}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{\\frac{8}{3}}^{2}}=\\frac{10}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=2+\\frac{10}{3}+2=\\frac{22}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564670 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1400ed01-a0a6-55a6-a62b-81de67ec5459" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 + 12 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564658} {:answer/id #uuid "7ea783a3-7345-5590-afc8-e2f042480069" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564691} {:answer/id #uuid "80997fb7-9f5a-58a7-8cc0-4a9b9477ef0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 + 6 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564692} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf715ae-835b-59a4-ad34-21a1d762f10e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\pi + 24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564695} {:answer/id #uuid "e7d5c7cb-3b29-56e2-b316-e056114bfe86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80997fb7-9f5a-58a7-8cc0-4a9b9477ef0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 + 6 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564692} :answer-field/id #uuid "b41b107d-cbf3-5a79-aad3-73a1033874fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564709}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3be3b093-65d3-5ad8-9987-edb100cd2356" :question/problem "![](images/69/69ff60a180694c898c1ae208d6e2dd95ef82ec0f27b7e4c1cc0256a04ae696b9.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is a path that traverses a semicircle of radius $6$ once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/96/964e6b51949b7162cfcd71f047b85980ef6387fb8268865a93b38183c060e844.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is a semi-circle of radius $r=6.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\pi r=6 \\pi .\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is a line segment of length $12.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=12.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=6 \\pi+12=6(\\pi+2).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564672 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "315d6a3a-bf07-5695-aa6d-9283f74a6fb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13 \\sqrt{2}}{3} + \\frac{13 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564665} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb601af-2f97-5f0a-9f49-9570729131f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13 \\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564676} {:answer/id #uuid "5a06c911-5b2b-5b9f-9d82-6303b8ae8fa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13 \\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564680} {:answer/id #uuid "67a526f3-3609-58d6-877d-5d77e6ffa487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13 \\pi}{6} + \\frac{26 \\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564683} {:answer/id #uuid "fa4567d7-c42b-5422-bf04-872ca010ce42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13 \\sqrt{2}}{3} + \\frac{13 \\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa4567d7-c42b-5422-bf04-872ca010ce42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13 \\sqrt{2}}{3} + \\frac{13 \\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564722} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e5e21c9-fef1-5528-9af8-b33dccbe4e58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "411a4ed7-09d4-5168-8b77-a42a36886e18" :question/problem "![](images/2a/2ae1eeb848f8d01597ec509c095d8a0307805640690d9d65102909e2b861e5d2.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/1e/1ec516fa1aa0172ba521d53fc11abd6268cac8eda4d1f221b741d5d9049dda99.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path shown above.\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is a quarter of a circle of radius $r=\\frac{13}{3}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{1}{4}(2\\pi r)=\\frac{13 \\pi}{6} .\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle where both legs have a length of $\\frac{13}{3}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{\\frac{13}{3}}^{2}+{\\frac{13}{3}}^{2}}=\\frac{13 \\sqrt{2}}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{13 \\pi}{6}+\\frac{13 \\sqrt{2}}{3}=\\frac{13}{6}(\\pi+2\\sqrt{2}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564673 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b2c3990-098b-5ab0-9aba-fc2d02824443" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{33 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564657} {:answer/id #uuid "26afed18-8d28-5c6b-87a4-7b956d517b25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564663} {:answer/id #uuid "48b164d4-5cf3-5793-85be-edf290d1e4ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11 + \\frac{33 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564675} {:answer/id #uuid "50b7e2c4-ecf8-5b64-b905-286e98efb4d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22 + \\frac{33 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564678} {:answer/id #uuid "75128e4d-afc1-58c3-a587-2af26df50270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11 + 33 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48b164d4-5cf3-5793-85be-edf290d1e4ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11 + \\frac{33 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564675} :answer-field/id #uuid "b38821a3-b0c7-5f00-86ae-85fd1c6ced4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "41dc3e1b-be2d-5bbc-86e9-c64fede51631" :question/problem "![](images/1a/1aad44e8db3ab56b858a003aada2ea280b879365de13842d7a41f9d7f89e822f.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/02/022aa19e71aed46d212400b6e403406fe3d21a657bd5b45eb23f00fbd32156eb.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is three-quarters of a circle of radius $r=11.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{3}{4}(2\\pi r)=\\frac{33 \\pi}{2} .\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is a line segment of length $11.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=11.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{33 \\pi}{2}+11.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564679 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05cb0d74-f33b-5fbe-8029-cbdbf413f5a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564655} {:answer/id #uuid "1e1dfdee-ccb2-5113-b159-0eb59c429284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16 \\sqrt{2}}{3} + \\frac{8 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564661} {:answer/id #uuid "485709c3-2695-52d5-b4d9-a7f3aefc9bea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 \\pi}{3} + \\frac{32 \\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564674} {:answer/id #uuid "50087344-4e93-533f-aa5c-aea54804ca54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16 \\sqrt{2}}{3} + \\frac{16 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564677} {:answer/id #uuid "73948027-cf11-5670-8e1d-5170c0721d7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16 \\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e1dfdee-ccb2-5113-b159-0eb59c429284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16 \\sqrt{2}}{3} + \\frac{8 \\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564661} :answer-field/id #uuid "3feca9ba-462f-5a07-b949-e027880efd04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "54958be3-5ebb-5406-b88b-f50f7f7a0951" :question/problem "![](images/e0/e028416a02722d1d832c2daddddbb23a314694ddd328670ed58376681dc7c023.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/5d/5d932a90da98448134bdb2deb9b524636ef7ad9aa59a7e91f9fe0d75178f395e.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path shown above.\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is a quarter of a circle of radius $r=\\frac{16}{3}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{1}{4}(2\\pi r)=\\frac{8 \\pi}{3} .\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle where both legs have a length of $\\frac{16}{3}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{\\frac{16}{3}}^{2}+{\\frac{16}{3}}^{2}}=\\frac{16 \\sqrt{2}}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{8 \\pi}{3}+\\frac{16 \\sqrt{2}}{3}=\\frac{8}{3}(\\pi+2\\sqrt{2}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564699 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ae28349-c307-508a-868f-e8da5aff759e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{37}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564669} {:answer/id #uuid "6b972325-d91a-5e10-a6a0-7673280cc2a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564686} {:answer/id #uuid "709a7d3e-e626-5446-b05f-99ddea8a8a89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{37} + 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564687} {:answer/id #uuid "de5cc153-16a5-5896-a764-ef96a7588c4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 + 2 \\sqrt{37}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564715} {:answer/id #uuid "fada5617-6d0a-523e-aacd-a9ac36a57c08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{37} + 20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "709a7d3e-e626-5446-b05f-99ddea8a8a89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{37} + 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564687} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4ae82dd-412c-55cf-9103-6de711e9a71c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564711}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "998321a9-810c-52e0-b273-f92be0787403" :question/problem "![](images/d6/d6128159e1606c72588f4881db5156ec3b73be224c160c15a0977a1eb1f824fa.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/2e/2e4d02399788c449b02d77757c66eb3be78e38289f0af5eac3ae784b5d0f2f5d.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $8$ and $6.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{6}^{2}}=10.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $1$ and $6.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{6}^{2}}=\\sqrt{37}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=10+\\sqrt{37}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564707 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3458a9b8-cdbc-5786-bf2f-2b7ac0f4648d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564666} {:answer/id #uuid "a249052d-2b98-5d71-8cc6-7047b84e12c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564703} {:answer/id #uuid "a2ac45a0-039d-5a49-a094-b47ec77bdc33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564704} {:answer/id #uuid "a820220a-b885-59b7-875d-3f6bb82842c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564705} {:answer/id #uuid "eda40aa1-5495-5e53-b669-a9ec57816c2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a820220a-b885-59b7-875d-3f6bb82842c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564705} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f8448eb-51b3-5597-a7b5-44b390db4b5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564701}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ac4e161a-9336-5d75-a616-039b5d8c09c1" :question/problem "![](images/26/26b263723ce79bb4ddb59ceac1f179447430b3cf8c3d14e3ea0dfc7612fc0665.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of three parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/55/553abb9d23d0a9e5f6b980e0c6418404881db984b6180caab1f0624d2deb9397.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe paths ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are line segments of length $8.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{3}}\\,\\text{d}s=8.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $8$ and $6.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{6}^{2}}=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=8+10+8=26.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564717 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e1298ec-a4c1-5df3-be99-ba930b16d915" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564660} {:answer/id #uuid "376127e0-f21c-5548-b2e1-55245e36fa29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22 + 11 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564667} {:answer/id #uuid "5d0f384f-05a3-5af8-9869-380f5efeb408" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11 \\pi + 44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564681} {:answer/id #uuid "8f9a4d3d-a7ed-5164-bc8d-a992b2ce65f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564697} {:answer/id #uuid "e2a1c553-f73e-51d3-9476-761da45de6a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22 + 22 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "376127e0-f21c-5548-b2e1-55245e36fa29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22 + 11 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564667} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5575d2e-bf63-5160-9f72-babb74586c2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564713}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e5898e01-d74e-5a4e-bea2-7c03b62c4e22" :question/problem "![](images/35/35cb0f44f9b2b88a56351a295c9b1d4de93674d10d914c3017e8fd9382d1e446.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is a path that traverses a semicircle of radius $11$ once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/bd/bdc6176ad2a20edab8ce185794c48dcb426828f561bceadddc3b3cb2e693fb62.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is a semi-circle of radius $r=11.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\pi r=11 \\pi .\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is a line segment of length $22.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=22.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=11 \\pi+22=11(\\pi+2).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564724 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b3cc87c-7837-5272-af3c-85f049ceebe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564659} {:answer/id #uuid "8bce55ea-29a7-58c1-8983-956eb2c3dd76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{37}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564693} {:answer/id #uuid "b6211ce5-73f6-5b8d-a813-90bb24c9ada2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564710} {:answer/id #uuid "c9e5b32a-1bff-5228-b5b1-84ac3f3e6e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564712} {:answer/id #uuid "e7adcb95-bcf9-5d59-b9d2-6219b2002b48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bce55ea-29a7-58c1-8983-956eb2c3dd76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{37}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564693} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ebcd7e0-473d-5535-bde9-0ad95533cc43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564682}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "fbcb1b60-1072-56e6-92d0-39f4e15df49b" :question/problem "![](images/24/249efb9fbaa6cc4f1bd923dd5aaa93d149cc07c56e23eb8ba12870b16c9108d3.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of three parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/20/20f9c299762ace89c0d0f8db158d6c8cedf266c5a08ad580c314a7d964897596.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe paths ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are line segments of length $6.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{3}}\\,\\text{d}s=6.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $6$ and $\\frac{5}{2}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{\\frac{5}{2}}^{2}}=\\frac{13}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=6+\\frac{13}{2}+6=\\frac{37}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718638 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90cd42af-267b-5875-bb15-bd56c1b5f751" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718645} {:answer/id #uuid "aa5a66e9-2339-5c37-aecc-046026859088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718646} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2ebc23-0fbe-5f8f-a40a-19a5d6440ac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718649} {:answer/id #uuid "df3fdbb5-e1f9-51cf-b998-2c493b6ae614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718650} {:answer/id #uuid "e67dd7e9-cdd1-5e69-a771-6aa631803dae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e67dd7e9-cdd1-5e69-a771-6aa631803dae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718651} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d77f875-8e0c-52f5-925e-97905db0c616" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "38246601-aa92-5ddc-abf5-04a09da1de9a" :question/problem "![Upper semicircle with diameter endpoints A(-1,1) and B(5,1)](images/de/dec59c468bd95a9e3e641209b688a1fa0c0cb6fa0d078730d87653820e2cce7e.png)\n\nCalculate\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the upper semicircular arc with diameter $AB$, traversed once from $B$ to $A$. The dashed diameter is a guide, not part of the path." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length equals the length $L$ of the path:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe endpoints of the diameter are $A(-1,1)$ and $B(5,1)$. Since they have the same $y$-coordinate,\n\n$$\nd=AB=5-(-1)=6,\\qquad r=\\frac{d}{2}=3.\n$$\n\nThe length of the semicircular arc is half the circumference:\n\n$$\nL=\\frac{1}{2}(2\\pi r)=3\\pi.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s=3\\pi.\n$$\n\nThe diameter is not traversed. Reversing direction would leave the arc length unchanged."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718641 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "090c33fa-cf9e-54a9-8ec2-feb4a3ad88a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718633} {:answer/id #uuid "2b6ff450-2f4d-5f4f-a41a-d3bf8b3965d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718637} {:answer/id #uuid "81b52b6a-1ca2-53cd-b8d2-26a3f063da2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718643} {:answer/id #uuid "bd7ee00b-2df8-5e76-a4c3-a2e5d5713bce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\pi\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718648} {:answer/id #uuid "ed2285ce-66b6-5116-9016-d86d66f1fa1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b6ff450-2f4d-5f4f-a41a-d3bf8b3965d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718637} :answer-field/id #uuid "51acb1a3-d272-5c6c-8316-3b64c1108a0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718640}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "527f107a-9fa1-58fb-8948-3a1234bf8e02" :question/problem "![Clockwise circle with diagonal diameter from A(-2,-1) to B(2,3)](images/8e/8e7bb5ef8527a97d61481cd545dbbeb4a30ef383b8f8fa273aee9061d1472f2d.png)\n\nCalculate\n\n$$\n\\oint_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the circle with diameter $AB$, traversed once clockwise. The dashed segment $AB$ is a guide, not part of the path." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length equals the length $L$ of the path:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nFirst find the diameter using the endpoint coordinates. The right triangle below is an auxiliary construction, not an additional path:\n\n![Right triangle with horizontal and vertical legs of length 4 along diameter AB](images/df/df4ccec99dcb2e5bc87533203c10475d5052c1dbc46ee699c4ce5f7d3695e7fb.png)\n\nThe coordinate differences are $2-(-2)=4$ and $3-(-1)=4$. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd=AB&=\\sqrt{(2-(-2))^2+(3-(-1))^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{4^2+4^2}=4\\sqrt{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA full traversal has length equal to the circumference:\n\n$$\nL=\\pi d=4\\pi\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\oint_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s=4\\pi\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nA closed path has zero net displacement, but its arc length is positive. Clockwise traversal does not make an integral with respect to $s$ negative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718644 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09cab807-35e2-5156-bace-cd568d7bd2e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718634} {:answer/id #uuid "14f98794-c72e-54c6-9c19-670f451b3cfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718635} {:answer/id #uuid "49713b10-a6eb-5df5-9858-dbde6e0014b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718639} {:answer/id #uuid "5848dad4-9b50-5fb4-aee4-995298f95473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718642} {:answer/id #uuid "ac4be79e-f39e-50c4-9984-612315619428" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49713b10-a6eb-5df5-9858-dbde6e0014b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718639} :answer-field/id #uuid "fda913f9-9bfc-5648-95b7-bac95a418f00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718653}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "87f72e02-2150-54e7-a38e-3cb9d2a4dc70" :question/problem "![Semicircle of radius 2 with counterclockwise arrows](images/24/244e830a32373fc20379f9b55650452c77e1a422ce5ee9456007cdac0d0daebc.png)\n\nCalculate\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the semicircular arc of radius $2$ shown above, traversed once counterclockwise." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length equals the length $L$ of the path:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nHere $C$ is half of a circle of radius $2$, so\n\n$$\nL=\\frac{1}{2}(2\\pi r)=\\pi(2)=2\\pi.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s=2\\pi.\n$$\n\nOnly the curved arc is traversed; the radius drawn as a dashed guide is not part of $C$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718764 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "065d293d-62e8-530c-a43d-6c7d20d4d71f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi+4\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718759} {:answer/id #uuid "366adb72-446e-54be-a79d-057dbf2cc41d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi+2\\sqrt{5}+4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718763} {:answer/id #uuid "8d35269d-ed4a-5b1d-9e0c-61282755658f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\pi+2\\sqrt{5}+4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718770} {:answer/id #uuid "cccaabbf-2b02-55ba-b749-bac529f5f9a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718773} {:answer/id #uuid "fb598ce3-23ce-524d-85af-c01c5ff385f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "366adb72-446e-54be-a79d-057dbf2cc41d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi+2\\sqrt{5}+4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718763} :answer-field/id #uuid "701ad14c-7605-5911-8b4c-1fc1f2b4054b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "48add826-1240-58c0-af1f-b2af8adce870" :question/problem "![](images/be/bebc358e1c941a03af63acc51e653bfda72ca5d5e4519a325b20c6c8341cc240.png)\n\nCalculate\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s,\n$$\nwhere $C$ is the closed path shown, traversed once in the direction of the arrows. The curved part from $B$ to $A$ is a semicircle with diameter $AB$; the other two parts are straight segments." :question/worked-solution "The three pieces are the semicircular arc $C_1$, the segment $AD$ labeled $C_2$, and the segment $DB$ labeled $C_3$:\n\n![](images/54/541c8d8ad7b5905709270e8774e874fc70063984cf6be9014cd158095e36c848.png)\n\nThe line integral of unity equals the total path length, so\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s=L_1+L_2+L_3.\n$$\n\nThe diameter has endpoints $A(-2,1)$ and $B(4,1)$. Its length is $4-(-2)=6$, so the radius is $3$ and\n\n$$\nL_1=\\frac12(2\\pi\\cdot3)=3\\pi.\n$$\n\nUse the distance formula separately for the two straight pieces. With $D(0,-3)$,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL_2&=\\sqrt{(0-(-2))^2+(-3-1)^2}=\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt{5},\\\\\nL_3&=\\sqrt{(4-0)^2+(1-(-3))^2}=\\sqrt{32}=4\\sqrt{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s=3\\pi+2\\sqrt{5}+4\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nThe diameter drawn with a dashed line is a construction aid, not part of $C$. Each of the three path lengths contributes positively."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718772 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1956e7db-f293-52c9-b72b-70095ab57383" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718762} {:answer/id #uuid "722eb938-709f-5245-9f0e-325f380b6176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\pi+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718769} {:answer/id #uuid "91172524-2c30-5f61-a1c8-1029ce22ffb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718771} {:answer/id #uuid "d27cdf4f-5089-5ed0-813c-73509023a157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718774} {:answer/id #uuid "e981f44f-4f85-5d9f-accb-7c016dcd17ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e981f44f-4f85-5d9f-accb-7c016dcd17ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718775} :answer-field/id #uuid "100c156c-bfbe-5804-ad9e-b550b8be472e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "af60db08-b062-55bc-a16c-17b1cc6b076b" :question/problem "![](images/ef/efd46d59336f6f2039e89f58cd330158324f255264d48bb943dfbaf40fd8239f.png)\n\nCalculate\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s,\n$$\nwhere $C$ follows the upper semicircle of radius $3$ and then its diameter, once in the direction of the arrows." :question/worked-solution "The path has two pieces, as shown below:\n\n![](images/eb/eb33864bcf8b11f8393dbf2425519f329667e39fbf8eb1b61bfd4543b3d143ff.png)\n\nThe line integral of unity equals the path's length. Additivity gives\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{C_1}\\,\\mathrm{d}s+\\int_{C_2}\\,\\mathrm{d}s.\n$$\n\nThe semicircular arc $C_1$ has length $\\frac12(2\\pi\\cdot3)=3\\pi$. The diameter $C_2$ has length $2\\cdot3=6$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s=3\\pi+6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718777 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03cba1e1-344a-5405-9a21-40046f88ac74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi+3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718758} {:answer/id #uuid "0b70baf0-edc3-56a4-bb73-46c360ff5ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718760} {:answer/id #uuid "59f59db7-342b-51cb-a2b8-5d4e7b0acd5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}-3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718765} {:answer/id #uuid "6ecda7f2-5404-5ac8-988f-b753a3bece6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718766} {:answer/id #uuid "ee67105f-7363-529d-bd28-3fb9e902aa04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}+3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee67105f-7363-529d-bd28-3fb9e902aa04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}+3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718776} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f3def2c-79be-523e-b701-b9407342d09a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f166d21e-a0b0-5de8-91b5-84f57909990e" :question/problem "![](images/c8/c824023213be3c003f60fd409b7812d43d21634ccbd1679586d4d76b191fe3e7.png)\n\nCalculate\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s,\n$$\nwhere $C$ follows the quarter-circle arc of radius $3$ centered at the origin, then the straight chord joining its endpoints, once in the direction of the arrows." :question/worked-solution "Split the path into the quarter-circle arc $C_1$ and the chord $C_2$:\n\n![](images/dc/dc02578579c30837a8f7041f87fa339fe708602f767f9cfc565b58a93cbb1d40.png)\n\nSince $\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s$ is the total length, add the two lengths. The quarter-circle arc has length\n\n$$\nL_1=\\frac14(2\\pi\\cdot3)=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe chord joins $(0,3)$ to $(3,0)$. By the distance formula,\n\n$$\nL_2=\\sqrt{(3-0)^2+(0-3)^2}=\\sqrt{18}=3\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\mathrm{d}s=L_1+L_2=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}+3\\sqrt{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718784 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45e559cf-1e28-53f6-834a-b6e859b40c82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718787} {:answer/id #uuid "aed3bebb-f859-5955-9b3a-bb007e234718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45e559cf-1e28-53f6-834a-b6e859b40c82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718787} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d670428-835b-5ea0-9de7-fe65880e3ee3" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-6$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718797} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ce06b0c-a166-5131-8901-226c4f40692d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718782} {:answer/id #uuid "5605bc5f-f9b6-54f0-a94f-14a93cf7a30a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ce06b0c-a166-5131-8901-226c4f40692d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718782} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebb75bdf-da8f-55a2-9324-6441fdefe4cf" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718802} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66a6988e-053d-59b3-8e16-7edd20f368fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718793} {:answer/id #uuid "dedfa3a3-92f1-5150-8a5c-859b0efa01ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dedfa3a3-92f1-5150-8a5c-859b0efa01ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718801} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa964994-706a-5014-b822-34d92dda902c" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "34a20438-75ac-56da-9e15-67462750db79" :question/problem "Consider the curves\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nC_1:\\quad \\mathbf r_1(t)&=\\langle t,t^2\\rangle, &0\\le t\\le 2,\\\\\nC_2:\\quad \\mathbf r_2(u)&=\\langle 2u,4u^2\\rangle, &0\\le u\\le 1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSuppose $f$ is continuous along the curves and\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-3.\n$$\n\nThe notation $-C_1$ means $C_1$ with its orientation reversed. Which statements must be true? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For $C_1$, eliminating $t$ gives $y=x^2$ with $0\\le x\\le 2$. For $C_2$, $x=2u$ gives $y=4u^2=x^2$, again with $0\\le x\\le 2$. Both trace this entire parabolic arc once, in the same direction; equivalently, $\\mathbf r_2(u)=\\mathbf r_1(2u)$.\n\nIndependence of parametrization gives\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-3.\n$$\n\nChanging parameter speed does not multiply this value by $2$, so the proposed value $-6$ is incorrect. Independence of orientation also gives\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-3,\n$$\n\nso the proposed value $3$ is incorrect. Select only the statement with $\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-3$. A scalar line integral may be negative when $f$ takes negative values; the nonnegative arc-length element does not force the integral to be positive."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718788 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ebc7c42-e7d6-5962-abe4-72b50dd93e9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718783} {:answer/id #uuid "3c1ccdcc-cf0a-5eeb-9104-627c9b79689b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718785} {:answer/id #uuid "615eaf13-2cfd-51ee-b2d8-3dd01ac3ec41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718792} {:answer/id #uuid "6dfac2e6-e439-50e4-8668-0f77c8ea5a5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dfac2e6-e439-50e4-8668-0f77c8ea5a5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718794} :answer-field/id #uuid "44184592-16a8-57eb-a299-9c32c8fdfcd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718786}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "50893ffd-9138-5cfe-bb3a-272da37be841" :question/problem "The diagram shows a curve $C$ from $A$ to $B$ and the same curve $-C$ traversed from $B$ to $A$. Each path traverses the curve once.\n\n![The same curve with opposite orientations: C from A to B and -C from B to A.](images/e4/e4f68e10429fa4bda69366751c303216d27df995edf2502b61ab9bfe84c3ff45.png)\n\nSuppose $f$ is continuous along the curve and\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=6.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $\\int_{-C} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s$?" :question/worked-solution "A scalar line integral with respect to arc length is independent of orientation. Reversing the arrows does not change the arc-length element $\\mathrm{d}s$ or the values of $f$ along the curve. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=6.\n$$\n\nThe answer is $6$. Reversing orientation does not negate the integral, cancel it, or count the curve twice."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718798 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1665fcdb-1fe5-5905-9be2-ec3d3e21e59b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718780} {:answer/id #uuid "cea17b0f-71c6-5abe-ab0c-ef3f6ae3fb43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1665fcdb-1fe5-5905-9be2-ec3d3e21e59b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718780} :answer-field/id #uuid "1492195b-c9d8-543b-b34d-369df22c8ba1" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718779} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92f398d1-92f9-587b-ab21-cf09f0b9940b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718796} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a41898-e50a-5c25-8a32-51e225d3b338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1a41898-e50a-5c25-8a32-51e225d3b338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718803} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f0490d4-14ae-516e-9283-3c699d054261" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718781} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60c061b9-5aa7-5899-8c56-9b591d0cbab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718791} {:answer/id #uuid "71ac83c7-19cb-5027-ac37-7209b5153222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60c061b9-5aa7-5899-8c56-9b591d0cbab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718791} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a47bcc7-71f6-5534-a0a3-83cb29b4852a" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\frac{2k}{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718790}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a8329369-6574-5a80-b05a-aedc3199e33a" :question/problem "The curve $C_1$ is parametrized by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_1(t)=\\langle\\sqrt{1+9t^2},3t\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le t\\le \\frac13$. The curve $C_2$ is parametrized by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_2(u)=\\langle\\sqrt{1+(1-2u)^2},1-2u\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le \\frac12$.\n\nSuppose $f$ is continuous along the curves and\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=k.\n$$\n\nThe notation $-C_2$ means $C_2$ with its orientation reversed. Which statements must be true for every such $f$? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For $C_1$, $y=3t$, so $x=\\sqrt{1+y^2}$ and $y$ increases from $0$ to $1$. For $C_2$, $y=1-2u$, so $x=\\sqrt{1+y^2}$ and $y$ decreases from $1$ to $0$. Thus both trace exactly once the same branch and interval,\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{1+y^2},\\qquad 0\\le y\\le 1,\n$$\n\nwith opposite orientations. In particular,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_2(u)=\\mathbf r_1\\!\\left(\\frac{1-2u}{3}\\right).\n$$\n\nA scalar line integral with respect to arc length is independent of both parametrization and orientation. Hence\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=k.\n$$\n\nReversing $C_2$ once more also preserves the value:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=k.\n$$\n\nThe parameter change has derivative $-2/3$, but this is not a factor multiplying the line integral: the speed factor in $\\mathrm{d}s$ and the parameter interval change together. The proposed value $2k/3$ is therefore not guaranteed. It agrees with $k$ when $k=0$, but fails, for example, when $f=1$ and $k$ is the positive length of this arc.\n\nSelect the statements with values $k$ on $C_2$ and on $-C_2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719127 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "763ce3a0-243c-5cea-b017-e67507f6a42e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 + 8 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719134} {:answer/id #uuid "ba9cdbe9-6b6d-5448-8825-84f868ae45b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 + 6 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719143} {:answer/id #uuid "c53d65b7-c670-5bca-afe4-b40829cc0b6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 + 4 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719144} {:answer/id #uuid "c990c3b7-3422-5869-8c1c-0c24aaccac79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\pi + 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719146} {:answer/id #uuid "d64ed336-b3b8-5845-8c11-446b53cc2c79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 + 8 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c53d65b7-c670-5bca-afe4-b40829cc0b6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 + 4 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719144} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5950f3e-a9b3-5094-9fb0-8947e33f8c07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "357da1f3-93bc-5bb2-bba0-b7815462deaa" :question/problem "![](images/a3/a3d47e0d43882ed83e4ea0fd7a137c4be00fda055217afede84a140bf347d671.png)\n\nCalculate\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ follows the semicircular arc and then its diameter, once in the direction of the arrows. The circular arc has radius $4$ and center $(0,1)$. The straight part joins $A(-4,1)$, $B(4,1)$." :question/worked-solution "The **line integral of unity** is the total path length. Split the path into its 2 pieces:\n\n![](images/09/0925e2d997ce37c69d51c7a5c58f30a335b6fb1501d6d852efc447b106aa70e3.png)\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=L_1+L_2.\n$$\n\nThe circular piece contributes\n\n$$\nL_1=\\frac12(2\\pi\\cdot 4)=4 \\pi.\n$$\n\nUse the distance formula for the straight pieces:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL_2&=\\sqrt{(4-(-4))^2+(1-(1))^2}=8.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd every traversed length positively:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=4 \\pi+8=8 + 4 \\pi.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719140 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "139dd2b0-0685-5cf6-b6e6-b1d949a7c765" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7 + \\frac{7 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719125} {:answer/id #uuid "9acc222b-2bf6-5883-9f2e-3d1ab369e170" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7 \\pi}{2} + 14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719139} {:answer/id #uuid "e4b54e6f-4712-5413-beb7-a9a777ea00e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14 + 7 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719151} {:answer/id #uuid "ef31c8f1-a63c-5a4f-8bb5-996a302f383e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7 + 7 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719153} {:answer/id #uuid "f264d43f-dc22-5ee6-92e2-bf579b61e3dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28 + 14 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4b54e6f-4712-5413-beb7-a9a777ea00e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14 + 7 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719151} :answer-field/id #uuid "109b2786-25f4-5b91-bdd6-e7b161878e57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719124}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a24bc8ab-4cfe-5a29-ad5a-cb2fce76b8e8" :question/problem "![](images/ac/ac9cb52534c444da338247543927c7b2efad546fd9dfa5ecae635e83768e16c3.png)\n\nCalculate\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ follows the semicircular arc and then its diameter, once in the direction of the arrows. The circular arc has radius $7$ and center $(0,1)$. The straight part joins $A(-7,1)$, $B(7,1)$." :question/worked-solution "The **line integral of unity** is the total path length. Split the path into its 2 pieces:\n\n![](images/be/be822384fab36cd1ac63c091e42faaedc4dc307529a1a668111a3c6a6ad3bcc0.png)\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=L_1+L_2.\n$$\n\nThe circular piece contributes\n\n$$\nL_1=\\frac12(2\\pi\\cdot 7)=7 \\pi.\n$$\n\nUse the distance formula for the straight pieces:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL_2&=\\sqrt{(7-(-7))^2+(1-(1))^2}=14.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd every traversed length positively:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=7 \\pi+14=14 + 7 \\pi.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719141 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "223a0957-8b18-586c-8d5a-d4f9d729a4be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 + 10 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719126} {:answer/id #uuid "3980b41e-6637-5721-bb6d-ea520fb7e51b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 + \\frac{15 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719128} {:answer/id #uuid "3bddb547-3c25-5f52-93e5-041d6d620773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 + \\frac{15 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719129} {:answer/id #uuid "6aec6405-2f5f-5535-8198-17b8f2173939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 + 15 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719132} {:answer/id #uuid "f6c775b0-0f8c-5897-ba18-d54aec84d5e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 + 15 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bddb547-3c25-5f52-93e5-041d6d620773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 + \\frac{15 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719129} :answer-field/id #uuid "dac1af50-2057-5f4b-8f9f-d31006540572" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a95f0ba5-8c07-5203-be92-934d76248d82" :question/problem "![](images/ff/ff6a09145d9dc2ac55a5c8733739f90745c8153e6c163e58c5e9494566542427.png)\n\nCalculate\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ follows the three-quarter-circle arc and then the horizontal segment, once in the direction of the arrows. The circular arc has radius $5$ and center $(0,0)$. The straight part joins $A(0,-5)$, $B(5,-5)$." :question/worked-solution "The **line integral of unity** is the total path length. Split the path into its 2 pieces:\n\n![](images/5b/5bb369ff483e884491e094ec520e74f8f3deebb970a21531b0c779d8e93b6f2f.png)\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=L_1+L_2.\n$$\n\nThe circular piece contributes\n\n$$\nL_1=\\frac34(2\\pi\\cdot 5)=\\frac{15 \\pi}{2}.\n$$\n\nUse the distance formula for the straight pieces:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL_2&=\\sqrt{(5-(0))^2+(-5-(-5))^2}=5.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd every traversed length positively:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\frac{15 \\pi}{2}+5=5 + \\frac{15 \\pi}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719152 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a964be7-326e-5852-b25a-a53f8660b387" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 + \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719130} {:answer/id #uuid "929dc75d-9474-5c6f-9255-8137b61c63ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1 + \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719138} {:answer/id #uuid "ccd2fb24-011d-5024-9d6e-c2dfa5706fd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719147} {:answer/id #uuid "d8b796cf-f332-5b3d-99c4-a515df0bd33c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 + \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719149} {:answer/id #uuid "efffe2d0-c3ce-5933-b796-ac35598a70a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + 2 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719154}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccd2fb24-011d-5024-9d6e-c2dfa5706fd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719147} :answer-field/id #uuid "896a2feb-c65e-5451-80ec-b41fb7e1fe7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719137}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e76c17f0-1807-5eb0-bcd3-8abd715db417" :question/problem "![](images/37/37d5d0a6b1ca2b4e3885b6bbe723f6826cead5a0ef7eb5277161c685d7ccbd05.png)\n\nCalculate\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ follows the three-quarter-circle arc and then the horizontal segment, once in the direction of the arrows. The circular arc has radius $1$ and center $(0,0)$. The straight part joins $A(0,-1)$, $B(1,-1)$." :question/worked-solution "The **line integral of unity** is the total path length. Split the path into its 2 pieces:\n\n![](images/c5/c57aee3e62e79d5c74c2c0e01e70d2a54f45e54cf535f73c10a77e6e7c1017d2.png)\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=L_1+L_2.\n$$\n\nThe circular piece contributes\n\n$$\nL_1=\\frac34(2\\pi\\cdot 1)=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}.\n$$\n\nUse the distance formula for the straight pieces:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL_2&=\\sqrt{(1-(0))^2+(-1-(-1))^2}=1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd every traversed length positively:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}+1=1 + \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719155 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ceb6d25-81c8-5710-8916-1e44ecc52e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6 + 3 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719133} {:answer/id #uuid "84b6db69-2a19-5aff-96e6-76a7a571fcbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 + 3 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719135} {:answer/id #uuid "86376259-7000-5f43-80d1-4d110efe21ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\pi + 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719136} {:answer/id #uuid "c5fe0dc0-bf9d-564d-9c1c-4aeb34c6539e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719145} {:answer/id #uuid "f48593e4-f71c-5851-ab57-097acd7289c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 + \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84b6db69-2a19-5aff-96e6-76a7a571fcbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 + 3 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719135} :answer-field/id #uuid "65dbc2fe-8c30-5f7d-aec5-f102d0f0e67a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719131}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f21de748-0220-516f-b1e1-562fc1fcbff6" :question/problem "![](images/88/88063c9ad935a0f48653c9fefded6ed35ea8168956a76c5a9c523da6ac467185.png)\n\nCalculate\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ follows the semicircular arc and then its diameter, once in the direction of the arrows. The circular arc has radius $3$ and center $(0,1)$. The straight part joins $A(-3,1)$, $B(3,1)$." :question/worked-solution "The **line integral of unity** is the total path length. Split the path into its 2 pieces:\n\n![](images/a2/a29e3eb1db737d61a8a69047ccfac6ada966d4bf11d2b8aebf87071632480cd9.png)\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=L_1+L_2.\n$$\n\nThe circular piece contributes\n\n$$\nL_1=\\frac12(2\\pi\\cdot 3)=3 \\pi.\n$$\n\nUse the distance formula for the straight pieces:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL_2&=\\sqrt{(3-(-3))^2+(1-(1))^2}=6.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd every traversed length positively:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=3 \\pi+6=6 + 3 \\pi.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719165 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "774be609-21e6-5b5e-ace5-4a8916ce5556" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719185} {:answer/id #uuid "9d200a8b-f78c-59eb-a794-a56fb50469e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "774be609-21e6-5b5e-ace5-4a8916ce5556" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719185} :answer-field/id #uuid "341f0c1b-d113-528f-85f5-933b4e0380a9" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-\\frac{7}{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719167} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7b04c7f-51de-500d-a689-41aebd48d971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719206} {:answer/id #uuid "f87de421-8b88-562a-973a-6c2fec51ec5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f87de421-8b88-562a-973a-6c2fec51ec5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719207} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d016362-db3d-5ed3-9858-11c043f29276" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-7$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719178} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "438f5d1f-965d-5d6a-babb-23b4ff00ebda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719173} {:answer/id #uuid "cea9f069-d864-5dd2-a037-b8ed0897216c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "438f5d1f-965d-5d6a-babb-23b4ff00ebda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719173} :answer-field/id #uuid "b32492ca-4b90-5e00-9a52-26afeb6dac23" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-7$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719197}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "29b573f0-023e-596f-b92d-8ceb6b31ba4c" :question/problem "The curve $C_1$ is parametrized by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_1(t)=\\langle 2(t)^4-(t)^2,(t)\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le t\\le 2$. The curve $C_2$ is parametrized by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_2(u)=\\langle 2(1-3u)^4-(1-3u)^2,(1-3u)\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le \\frac{1}{3}$. Suppose $f$ is continuous along both curves and\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-7.\n$$\n\nA minus sign on a curve means its orientation is reversed. **Which statements must be true** for every such $f$? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Write points on the known curve in terms of a geometric parameter $z$:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf R(z)=\\langle 2(z)^4-(z)^2,(z)\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFor $C_1$, $z=t$ increases from $0$ to $2$. For $C_2$, $z=1-3u$ decreases from $1$ to $0$. Eliminating the parameter on $C_1$ gives $x=2y^4-y^2$. The other curve covers only the part with $0\\le z\\le 1$, rather than $0\\le z\\le 2$. A shared Cartesian equation alone is insufficient. A continuous function supported near an interior point of the omitted arc can be scaled to give any prescribed nonzero integral on the full curve, while its integral on the subarc stays zero. Thus no nonzero fixed multiple of the full integral is guaranteed on the subarc. \n\nReversing $C_1$ always preserves its value:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-7.\n$$\n\nChanging the parameter speed does not supply a multiplicative factor. \n\nStatement 1, $\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-7$, is **true**. Statement 2, $\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-7$, is **not guaranteed**. Statement 3, $\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-\\frac{7}{3}$, is **not guaranteed**. "}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "030b0bf6-c95a-59fe-84fa-67dc367effe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719161} {:answer/id #uuid "79afdca9-20c4-5e1a-a94f-534d8dfe7580" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "030b0bf6-c95a-59fe-84fa-67dc367effe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719161} :answer-field/id #uuid "04f5c12b-c15e-5527-b6e0-6908ba44930b" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719162} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49dd4c01-41e8-5ae2-ac6f-42eb8d6d1082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719176} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e4e4bc-8e11-5eb0-9a4d-4669af2347c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49dd4c01-41e8-5ae2-ac6f-42eb8d6d1082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719176} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab310270-00af-514e-8894-98d2db798dc3" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=6$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719195} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e503bfc-9bab-5b63-b21a-521b37bfd25e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719163} {:answer/id #uuid "45279593-7dce-5158-82c2-b1b325d2386e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e503bfc-9bab-5b63-b21a-521b37bfd25e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719163} :answer-field/id #uuid "b05ed446-7106-5a6a-9dec-54f1a8f7a6ba" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6cb3eead-b136-5bef-b2ed-be2bd3c59f96" :question/problem "The curve $C_1$ is parametrized by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_1(t)=\\langle (t),2(t)^{3/2}\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le t\\le 2$. The curve $C_2$ is parametrized by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_2(u)=\\langle (1-2u),2(1-2u)^{3/2}\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le \\frac{1}{2}$. Suppose $f$ is continuous along both curves and\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=3.\n$$\n\nA minus sign on a curve means its orientation is reversed. **Which statements must be true** for every such $f$? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Write points on the known curve in terms of a geometric parameter $z$:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf R(z)=\\langle (z),2(z)^{3/2}\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFor $C_1$, $z=t$ increases from $0$ to $2$. For $C_2$, $z=1-2u$ decreases from $1$ to $0$. Eliminating the parameter on $C_1$ gives $y=2x^{3/2}$. The other curve covers only the part with $0\\le z\\le 1$, rather than $0\\le z\\le 2$. A shared Cartesian equation alone is insufficient. A continuous function supported near an interior point of the omitted arc can be scaled to give any prescribed nonzero integral on the full curve, while its integral on the subarc stays zero. Thus no nonzero fixed multiple of the full integral is guaranteed on the subarc. \n\nReversing $C_1$ always preserves its value:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=3.\n$$\n\nChanging the parameter speed does not supply a multiplicative factor. \n\nStatement 1, $\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=3$, is **true**. Statement 2, $\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=6$, is **not guaranteed**. Statement 3, $\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=3$, is **not guaranteed**. "}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719187 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3aee0bba-6e65-5f31-b4a3-49cb399419f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719170} {:answer/id #uuid "3ba9d2cf-6856-5fc2-8d68-c0266aea8ae7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ba9d2cf-6856-5fc2-8d68-c0266aea8ae7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719171} :answer-field/id #uuid "27aa5c54-6379-519c-b19e-6920bc87e512" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-6$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719164} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "665ed2e2-5812-5969-aeb7-edfebdf3c206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719181} {:answer/id #uuid "9c64bf3c-91d4-58f6-9e63-302761659a13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "665ed2e2-5812-5969-aeb7-edfebdf3c206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719181} :answer-field/id #uuid "686f200f-da72-5aa8-ac27-16392f242f00" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719183} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02dc03a9-c4bb-56dd-a2d1-6b4e83e38890" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719160} {:answer/id #uuid "ff2a61a0-1283-512e-9ba0-5102b1f47cde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02dc03a9-c4bb-56dd-a2d1-6b4e83e38890" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719160} :answer-field/id #uuid "d14ffb2e-7375-5a9b-b4ff-ba11c0a50998" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719202}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "91462a6f-bf0a-5ef5-8080-d78ff72774ac" :question/problem "The curve $C_2$ is parametrized by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_2(t)=\\langle 2(t)^4-(t)^2,(t)\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le t\\le 1$. The curve $C_1$ is parametrized by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_1(u)=\\langle 2(3u)^4-(3u)^2,(3u)\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le \\frac{1}{3}$. Suppose $f$ is continuous along both curves and\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-2.\n$$\n\nA minus sign on a curve means its orientation is reversed. **Which statements must be true** for every such $f$? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Write points on the known curve in terms of a geometric parameter $z$:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf R(z)=\\langle 2(z)^4-(z)^2,(z)\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFor $C_2$, $z=t$ increases from $0$ to $1$. For $C_1$, $z=3u$ increases from $0$ to $1$. Eliminating the parameter on $C_2$ gives $x=2y^4-y^2$. The other curve has the same locus, branch and full parameter range; both traverse the arc once. The parameter map is $t=(3u)/1$. Its sign controls direction, not the scalar integral. \n\nReversing $C_2$ always preserves its value:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-2.\n$$\n\nIndependence of parametrization and orientation also gives $\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-2$. Changing the parameter speed does not supply a multiplicative factor. \n\nStatement 1, $\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-6$, is **not guaranteed**. Statement 2, $\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-2$, is **true**. Statement 3, $\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-2$, is **true**. "}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53acb30f-14b0-5dca-82ea-2d009d16e05d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719179} {:answer/id #uuid "9ec4adf8-9d0e-5fac-b8d1-d003495116c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53acb30f-14b0-5dca-82ea-2d009d16e05d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719179} :answer-field/id #uuid "348afb3e-154e-53d2-8fdf-41e2da477ae9" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719168} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dd92ca7-5a8e-5c8f-b76b-1156cd2ee776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719166} {:answer/id #uuid "ea72c7b3-4e32-56eb-a60c-d5e43eb16d10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2dd92ca7-5a8e-5c8f-b76b-1156cd2ee776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719166} :answer-field/id #uuid "45299224-9f22-5c9e-8299-c83e24a00f6b" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719175} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "378aea8a-6875-5c2a-8723-c10e5e58099c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719169} {:answer/id #uuid "3f52a0ec-2543-584f-8bbd-ffe5424b800a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f52a0ec-2543-584f-8bbd-ffe5424b800a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719172} :answer-field/id #uuid "a975d381-1296-542a-b38d-15315d012080" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-6$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "968c5362-1777-5a9a-816a-eac915f50d72" :question/problem "The curve $C_2$ is parametrized by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_2(t)=\\langle 3\\cos(t),3\\sin(t)\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le t\\le \\pi$. The curve $C_1$ is parametrized by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_1(u)=\\langle 3\\cos(\\pi-3u),3\\sin(\\pi-3u)\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le \\frac{1}{3}\\pi$. Suppose $f$ is continuous along both curves and\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-2.\n$$\n\nA minus sign on a curve means its orientation is reversed. **Which statements must be true** for every such $f$? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Write points on the known curve in terms of a geometric parameter $z$:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf R(z)=\\langle 3\\cos(z),3\\sin(z)\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFor $C_2$, $z=t$ increases from $0$ to $\\pi$. For $C_1$, $z=\\pi-3u$ decreases from $\\pi$ to $0$. Eliminating the parameter on $C_2$ gives $x^2+y^2=9,\\quad y\\ge0$. The other curve has the same locus, branch and full parameter range; both traverse the arc once. The parameter map is $t=(\\pi-3u)/1$. Its sign controls direction, not the scalar integral. \n\nReversing $C_2$ always preserves its value:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-2.\n$$\n\nIndependence of parametrization and orientation also gives $\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-2$. Changing the parameter speed does not supply a multiplicative factor. \n\nStatement 1, $\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-6$, is **not guaranteed**. Statement 2, $\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-2$, is **true**. Statement 3, $\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=-2$, is **true**. "}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719192 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bc7a329-4a2d-52c0-9b13-ef66a8fc2ddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719177} {:answer/id #uuid "fd801e7d-a69e-559c-9844-d63e7bb384b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bc7a329-4a2d-52c0-9b13-ef66a8fc2ddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719177} :answer-field/id #uuid "5450d047-a4c3-576b-b332-12b1cd393ccf" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\frac{8}{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719180} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a87556a3-95ba-52f9-93ec-dfb19ab1ecce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719193} {:answer/id #uuid "dd44e581-cf7e-508f-885a-1f997c1b6ab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd44e581-cf7e-508f-885a-1f997c1b6ab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719204} :answer-field/id #uuid "6684b8ef-60af-51ad-8d19-d47fd2517f9c" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719182} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd1af1d7-47f4-5680-8e3e-108b60db9270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719198} {:answer/id #uuid "c8be6379-0726-5e03-895f-bc9ce33e53d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8be6379-0726-5e03-895f-bc9ce33e53d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719199} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc11af7f-0dc7-5c6d-af08-ab1beca2ecee" :answer-field/key "$\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a186908d-69ac-5378-9339-668e7f523a85" :question/problem "The curve $C_2$ is parametrized by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_2(t)=\\langle (t),3(t)^{3/2}\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le t\\le 2$. The curve $C_1$ is parametrized by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r_1(u)=\\langle (3u),3(3u)^{3/2}\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le \\frac{2}{3}$. Suppose $f$ is continuous along both curves and\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=8.\n$$\n\nA minus sign on a curve means its orientation is reversed. **Which statements must be true** for every such $f$? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Write points on the known curve in terms of a geometric parameter $z$:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf R(z)=\\langle (z),3(z)^{3/2}\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFor $C_2$, $z=t$ increases from $0$ to $2$. For $C_1$, $z=3u$ increases from $0$ to $2$. Eliminating the parameter on $C_2$ gives $y=3x^{3/2}$. The other curve has the same locus, branch and full parameter range; both traverse the arc once. The parameter map is $t=(3u)/1$. Its sign controls direction, not the scalar integral. \n\nReversing $C_2$ always preserves its value:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=8.\n$$\n\nIndependence of parametrization and orientation also gives $\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=8$. Changing the parameter speed does not supply a multiplicative factor. \n\nStatement 1, $\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=8$, is **true**. Statement 2, $\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=8$, is **true**. Statement 3, $\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\frac{8}{3}$, is **not guaranteed**. "}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719262 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b0d9ec-e480-5f4c-94ce-07194c4656a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719250} {:answer/id #uuid "27c3e3ea-3ecf-55cc-8909-4ee71ab12b3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719254} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4dae27-e080-5fcb-8eff-a93c85e0cc97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719255} {:answer/id #uuid "f71bd27f-c118-5b75-a4f6-b0f1f6f5f181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f71bd27f-c118-5b75-a4f6-b0f1f6f5f181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719270} :answer-field/id #uuid "640ac895-4093-50a3-9871-3bd508ade6d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719259}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "940ec211-0589-5e15-8227-91589d4c1e8a" :question/problem "The paths $C$ and $D$ trace exactly the same geometric arc once, in the same direction. The path $D$ follows $C$ in the same direction.\n\nThe parametrization of $D$ runs 2 times as fast, with its parameter interval shortened accordingly. Suppose $f$ is continuous along the arc and\n\n$$\n\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=7.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $\\int_{D} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s$?" :question/worked-solution "Scalar line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of parametrization and orientation. Both paths cover the same arc once, so\n\n$$\n\\int_{D} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=7.\n$$\n\nThe speed change is offset by the shortened parameter interval. Reversing direction does not negate the integral, and a single traversal does not cancel it. Neither multiplying nor dividing by the parameter speed is appropriate."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719263 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b57ce8e-e24b-556d-ad7d-c33e7fb40cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719252} {:answer/id #uuid "a67da445-3eaa-5651-8424-79345ccf026e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719265} {:answer/id #uuid "d42f9c13-9edc-5f8e-b05d-9a8d14578aa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719267} {:answer/id #uuid "e99f1c3d-53cf-5948-8fd0-d20fbb5f51fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e99f1c3d-53cf-5948-8fd0-d20fbb5f51fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719269} :answer-field/id #uuid "f83aaa0a-5fc6-5dbd-899f-06380bde5469" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719271}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "989ec26d-d8f3-5d82-9352-c40fa3d55710" :question/problem "The paths $C$ and $D$ trace exactly the same geometric arc once, in opposite directions. The path $D=-C$ is the reversed path in the diagram.\n\n![The same curve traversed in opposite directions.](images/e4/e4f68e10429fa4bda69366751c303216d27df995edf2502b61ab9bfe84c3ff45.png)\n\nThe parametrization of $D$ runs 2 times as fast, with its parameter interval shortened accordingly. Suppose $f$ is continuous along the arc and\n\n$$\n\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=4.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $\\int_{D} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s$?" :question/worked-solution "Scalar line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of parametrization and orientation. Both paths cover the same arc once, so\n\n$$\n\\int_{D} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=4.\n$$\n\nThe speed change is offset by the shortened parameter interval. Reversing direction does not negate the integral, and a single traversal does not cancel it. Neither multiplying nor dividing by the parameter speed is appropriate."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719264 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0116279a-24db-5eb6-a34c-7c568eec5140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719249} {:answer/id #uuid "17bcab41-7d65-5548-a075-bbaab45c3a79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719253} {:answer/id #uuid "5c61bbea-d6b8-567b-bb62-068412fd0ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719258} {:answer/id #uuid "8dfb5c5c-fea8-5bb1-8e80-279843f97ed1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8dfb5c5c-fea8-5bb1-8e80-279843f97ed1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719261} :answer-field/id #uuid "83e211d1-bbc4-5fe5-a2bd-e47e17ad7a28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719260}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9daddeac-3f3a-5204-a41d-f91a8603ffda" :question/problem "The paths $C$ and $D$ trace exactly the same geometric arc once, in the same direction. The path $D$ follows $C$ in the same direction.\n\nThe parametrization of $D$ runs 3 times as fast, with its parameter interval shortened accordingly. Suppose $f$ is continuous along the arc and\n\n$$\n\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=7.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $\\int_{D} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s$?" :question/worked-solution "Scalar line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of parametrization and orientation. Both paths cover the same arc once, so\n\n$$\n\\int_{D} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=7.\n$$\n\nThe speed change is offset by the shortened parameter interval. Reversing direction does not negate the integral, and a single traversal does not cancel it. Neither multiplying nor dividing by the parameter speed is appropriate."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719266 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57afaf01-5f83-5906-b287-6d183ff8c893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719256} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb06cb9-b268-56a7-8eba-c3c2cab404c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719257} {:answer/id #uuid "d7320568-87f8-5f34-a3c1-8f5b404e43aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719268} {:answer/id #uuid "f843d815-a8b4-5ffa-9187-a27580b469fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719272}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7320568-87f8-5f34-a3c1-8f5b404e43aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719268} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ada4732-e977-5d30-bcdc-a77b76d5eca1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719251}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bd50f534-886e-5866-928b-049f7894cca6" :question/problem "The paths $C$ and $D$ trace exactly the same geometric arc once, in opposite directions. The path $D=-C$ is the reversed path in the diagram.\n\n![The same curve traversed in opposite directions.](images/e4/e4f68e10429fa4bda69366751c303216d27df995edf2502b61ab9bfe84c3ff45.png)\n\nThe parametrization of $D$ runs 3 times as fast, with its parameter interval shortened accordingly. Suppose $f$ is continuous along the arc and\n\n$$\n\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=7.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $\\int_{D} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s$?" :question/worked-solution "Scalar line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of parametrization and orientation. Both paths cover the same arc once, so\n\n$$\n\\int_{D} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=7.\n$$\n\nThe speed change is offset by the shortened parameter interval. Reversing direction does not negate the integral, and a single traversal does not cancel it. Neither multiplying nor dividing by the parameter speed is appropriate."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719284 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16d49e6d-b9fa-5d9f-8145-d0d67f3ea18b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719285} {:answer/id #uuid "317fb102-3687-5e4a-bd13-4b913e1fc507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719290} {:answer/id #uuid "5edd47f8-f4fd-5b19-a3be-9a37b3c9d20a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719296} {:answer/id #uuid "7ce5fa91-0c80-5799-bbe3-2c2dbf0a8b88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719303} {:answer/id #uuid "fd3aa1b3-46f5-5279-912a-b532442a4d96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16d49e6d-b9fa-5d9f-8145-d0d67f3ea18b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719285} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b6b4e87-51b8-502b-9a29-c0b3517a5937" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0ee62fdf-2501-5d84-9a14-fd7d1a262da9" :question/problem "![Curve and its measurements](images/26/26ebfac5fbca51116e97437adee9e3c64f41a5055e6398bd3b594e3992e72517.png)\n\nCalculate\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment shown, traversed once from $B$ to $A$." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length equals the length $L$ of the path:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe endpoints are $A(2,-1)$ and $B(-6,-1)$. The segment is horizontal. Its endpoint distance is\n\n$$\nd=AB=|-6-(2)|=8.\n$$\n\nHere the path is the segment itself, so\n\n$$\nL=d=8.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=8.\n$$\n\nReversing the direction leaves traveled length unchanged."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719292 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00f9793d-adf9-57da-86d0-6795dafe0d41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719280} {:answer/id #uuid "2f7d573b-5a3f-591b-9fb2-e08419110c95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719289} {:answer/id #uuid "411a5bde-6cb3-544a-8086-ca683e489ab6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719293} {:answer/id #uuid "6ea7daaa-8767-5116-ae1d-e9135dba18f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719299} {:answer/id #uuid "847e83a9-795c-575f-b00e-d48ca6ff36af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "847e83a9-795c-575f-b00e-d48ca6ff36af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719305} :answer-field/id #uuid "984df103-3ed1-50d0-8ad9-2a2357de6cee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "33fd7fa5-7818-5345-8548-58ed3b91c129" :question/problem "![Curve and its measurements](images/d0/d0bb8c5625964fb0945e00cccf2e382dc69f5cb6fe40e2dea257fdb2191d7c8b.png)\n\nCalculate\n\n$$\n\\oint_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the circle with radius $5$ shown, traversed once clockwise. The dashed guide is not part of the path." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length equals the length $L$ of the path:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe supplied radius determines the diameter:\n\n$$\nd=2r=2(5)=10.\n$$\n\nThe path is a full circle. Its circumference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\pi d\\\\&=\\pi(10)=10 \\pi.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\oint_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=10 \\pi.\n$$\n\nReversing the direction leaves traveled length unchanged. A closed path has zero net displacement, but its length is positive."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719298 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47b19182-16cc-580e-bcf7-c27bdff5ae75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719294} {:answer/id #uuid "5b81bd33-d791-536a-a7f4-dcfa9113bd07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719295} {:answer/id #uuid "9a936ac7-b1f1-5969-9ced-edb4f858619a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719308} {:answer/id #uuid "f1037a43-65ac-5d7f-8ede-8cc88cd7ca7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719312} {:answer/id #uuid "f96825fc-30a0-5a3f-8125-6f751ae98525" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a936ac7-b1f1-5969-9ced-edb4f858619a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719308} :answer-field/id #uuid "837af8c9-a664-5435-b415-bfdc55d520e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719304}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "69a5ad13-edcf-5d2c-96c2-fba6862cdec2" :question/problem "![Curve and its measurements](images/52/52af9feefbf91f7b3f61290a39b5e421ef13c4cbe4f5d0528a51126dd939bb0b.png)\n\nCalculate\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment shown, traversed once from $A$ to $B$." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length equals the length $L$ of the path:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe endpoints are $A(0,-3)$ and $B(0,-10)$. The segment is vertical. Its endpoint distance is\n\n$$\nd=AB=|-10-(-3)|=7.\n$$\n\nHere the path is the segment itself, so\n\n$$\nL=d=7.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=7.\n$$\n\nReversing the direction leaves traveled length unchanged."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719310 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2961674c-deb0-5d7f-b52b-375f360c1b21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719287} {:answer/id #uuid "2d9e53c0-9884-572b-a5e6-afa162c4a805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719288} {:answer/id #uuid "333ecc8a-87a5-52bf-bae9-6488e6599100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 + 8 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719291} {:answer/id #uuid "6efc7591-2653-50d0-b100-bcb54bd59b00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719300} {:answer/id #uuid "77a592ff-00d1-566d-98fa-1820ba31e412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2961674c-deb0-5d7f-b52b-375f360c1b21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719287} :answer-field/id #uuid "926dd1e2-f321-5896-930f-cb42f6921f38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719306}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e66d13dc-e7e6-53e8-8872-9c87a4ad3156" :question/problem "![Curve and its measurements](images/3b/3be3d460f2800fcc90d02d617ee7c446b17c6fe5f25800081b7cd4f5ea9a3b36.png)\n\nCalculate\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the semicircular arc with radius $8$ shown, traversed once counterclockwise. The dashed guide is not part of the path." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length equals the length $L$ of the path:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe supplied radius determines the diameter:\n\n$$\nd=2r=2(8)=16.\n$$\n\nThe path is half of a circle. Using circumference from diameter,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\frac{\\pi d}{2}\\\\&=\\frac{\\pi(16)}{2}=8 \\pi.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=8 \\pi.\n$$\n\nReversing the direction leaves traveled length unchanged."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719311 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a11a4ed-614d-56c7-8c45-b45f7837eea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719281} {:answer/id #uuid "17034f4b-52c8-55b7-a90d-6d35ab263816" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{61}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719286} {:answer/id #uuid "6817745b-ca5d-5e0c-84e2-ad256afb1b73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719297} {:answer/id #uuid "6f92c0f0-ec0c-581a-ae07-3864f611cfe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719301} {:answer/id #uuid "d497352c-c590-59bf-8c59-4a45d45c2a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17034f4b-52c8-55b7-a90d-6d35ab263816" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{61}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719286} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d4f2226-ecfa-5e25-9d27-dff46302e344" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719283}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e73d524b-889b-5253-9bfa-ec9a69e21847" :question/problem "![Curve and its measurements](images/d2/d2a26cc541e294c54c14b2495ebc0a14bbd820721a510cd22c5bdb6e3a670559.png)\n\nCalculate\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment shown, traversed once from $B$ to $A$." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length equals the length $L$ of the path:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe endpoints are $A(1,2)$ and $B(6,8)$. The dotted right triangle is an auxiliary construction, not additional path.\n\n![Auxiliary right triangle](images/de/de466b36bcd7e3e39c77ba45055dba3d9fed3846d40940184e65a6fb8508d8bf.png)\n\nUse the two coordinate differences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d=AB&=\\sqrt{(6-(1))^2+(8-(2))^2}\\\\&=\\sqrt{25+36}=\\sqrt{61}=\\sqrt{61}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere the path is the segment itself, so\n\n$$\nL=d=\\sqrt{61}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\sqrt{61}.\n$$\n\nReversing the direction leaves traveled length unchanged."}]}
